1
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:46,039
-Bala, are you alright?
-I'm fine.

2
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,639
I'm fine.

3
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,319
-Gonca, are you alright? -I'm fine.

4
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,439
Didn't I kill you?

5
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,519
I cut you into pieces with my sword.

6
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:01,159
I threw you off the castle walls.

7
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,239
How is that possible?

8
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:07,039
How did you not die?

9
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,759
You demon with nine lives!

10
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,959
I'm here to finish
what I started, Osman.

11
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,359
The ground didn't accept you, huh?

12
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,519
I will bury you deep under the ground!

13
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:24,279
You will go under the ground, Osman.

14
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,439
I will make you go through...

15
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,399
...much worse than what you did to me.

16
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,119
I will...

17
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:40,599
...kill all of your family...

18
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,199
...one by one in pain.

19
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,599
First me before my family.

20
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,239
You have to get me first.

21
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:54,039
You vile dog.

22
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,919
Come here. Come.

23
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,559
You know what my sword tastes like,

24
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,399
...Sofia.

25
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,959
It won't be that easy, Osman.

26
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:08,599
-You will kneel this time. Soldiers!
-Alps! Attack!

27
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,519
Ya Allah

28
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:38,999
Bala, aren't you curious
about the secret I'll give you?

29
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,399
Keep your poisonous words to yourself, demon!

30
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,199
You won't live long this time.

31
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,879
I will kill you.

32
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:03,279
Praise be to my hatun. Come on!

33
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,559
I killed you.

34
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,359
You just don't know yet.

35
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,999
I'm here, mother!

36
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,279
Sofia...

37
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,679
Sofia, we need to go. We're losing.

38
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:29,799
What are you doing, Lukas? What?

39
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:45,199
Our soldiers are dying

40
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,959
-He has to die!
Yes, but not now!

41
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,919
If we stay, we'll lose! Let's go!

42
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,679
He has to die! He has to!
-Sofia!

43
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,439
Osman.

44
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:08,679
They're running off.

45
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:11,239
-They can't go anywhere.
-Let's go.

46
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:03,839
-Gonca, are you alright? -I'm fine.

47
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,599
Good. Come on!

48
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,479
Allah is the greatest!

49
00:09:15,289 --> 00:09:16,479
Gonca!

50
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,839
Begum Hatun...

51
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,279
Thank you.

52
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,159
Thank you, Begum Hatun.

53
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,639
I owe you a life now.

54
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:43,119
There's the sake of fight
between you and me.

55
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:45,399
So you owe me nothing.

56
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,239
Alaaddin!

57
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,879
Go after our father! Go!

58
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,759
Alright, brother!

59
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,639
Come on, alps! Let's go!

60
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:28,679
Come on, alps!

61
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,317
-Is everyone alright?
-I'm fine, my Bey.

62
00:10:43,329 --> 00:10:44,599
I'm good, my Shahzade.

63
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:48,439
Dastards who ambushed
Borus got what they deserved

64
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:49,599
Everyone is fine.

65
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,159
Thanks to Allah.

66
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,399
Alps, inform all the alps around Sogut.

67
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:58,479
Tell them to hold all the ways going
to the borders of Prusa and Byzantine.

68
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:00,399
-All of them.
-As you order, my Bey.

69
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,879
Let's go.

70
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:16,759
Sofia, you survived this time.

71
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,079
But you're walking to your death again.
-Osman. Osman!

72
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,119
Bala.

73
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:30,199
Bala, you have a wound.

74
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,799
What is this, Bala?

75
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:50,159
Bala. Bala.

76
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:58,479
Why didn't you tell me?
Why are you coming with us?

77
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,119
Alps, bring some bandages.

78
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,319
Give it to me. Come on, come on.

79
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:07,839
Oh Bala...

80
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:20,319
Lukas.

81
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:27,279
We were supposed to kill Kayi women
here while Osman was chasing a lie.

82
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:30,359
We were so close.

83
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:35,279
I swear both Osman and Bala
will regret that they didn't die today.

84
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:40,359
I will open a wound inside them
which is sharper than a sword.

85
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:44,359
They will beg me for mercy.

86
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:48,999
I know this wild look that would
scare even the devil himself.

87
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:55,599
I have a treasure which
is very valuable for Kayis...

88
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,639
...and which only I know about, Lukas.

89
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:04,159
Even the name of this treasure
will make Kayis kneel before me.

90
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:07,399
What is it, Sofia?

91
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:11,519
The chain I will put around
the neck of Kayis, Lukas.

92
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,679
Be patient, though.

93
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,199
You will see soon.

94
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,999
Let's not stay long here.

95
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:23,759
They may come any moment.

96
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:26,239
They must have held the road to the castle.

97
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,639
-You should use the other ways.
-You?

98
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,879
-Are you not coming?
-I will.

99
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:35,479
But I have a thing to do first.

100
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:55,559
The devil...

101
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,199
...who we thought was dead for so long.

102
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,199
Osman.

103
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,199
You killed Sofia with your own hands.
-Right.

104
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:11,479
All the cruelty she caused is
clear from the way she hid her face.

105
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:15,199
But she got out of hell.

106
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,519
She kept her grudge alive and
she is making plans against us.

107
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,959
She brought trouble...

108
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:24,599
...as soon as she came to the frontiers.

109
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,119
First Baysungur and his men...

110
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:29,959
...then Fatma.

111
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:33,359
Then you.

112
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:38,599
She knows well that if she touches my
daughter or you, I will cut her into pieces.

113
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,279
But remember.

114
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,119
She is not just an enemy.

115
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:45,879
Now she will attack us like a mad dog.

116
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,159
Come on, my Bey.

117
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,759
Let's go after her, let's go and kill her.

118
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:54,039
Bala, how can we do that?
No. Don't you see your wound?

119
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:58,079
First, your wound will heal.
Alright? You will be alright...

120
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:00,239
...then you will stand next to me.

121
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,679
-Alright.
-Bala...

122
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:08,079
She got out of hell...

123
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:10,799
She revived in fiery flames.

124
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,479
But we will drown her in her own blood.

125
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,679
We will drown her in her blood.

126
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:16,839
Son.

127
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:18,599
Come.

128
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,279
Mother, are you alright?

129
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:24,239
Come, check your mother's wounds.
-I am alright, my son.

130
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:27,479
I am alright.
No. No. We have to do something.

131
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:31,279
You've lost blood.

132
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,479
You will get weaker.

133
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,119
Let's go. Come on. -Come on.

134
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,639
Hold it here.

135
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,439
Hold this here.

136
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,439
My Bey..

137
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:51,359
We killed all the infidels.

138
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:55,519
But their owners... Did they run away, my Bey?

139
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:59,119
Neither they nor Karesi Bey...

140
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,719
None of them can escape
our wrath. None of them.

141
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,279
For sure, my Bey.

142
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:05,879
But...

143
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,999
That dog named Sofia...

144
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:12,359
Her mind works like the devil's.

145
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:15,799
Thus, we won't rush.
First, we will make our plan.

146
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,119
-Then we will set out.
-Yes my Bey. -Come on.

147
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:33,559
His wound is serious, and
he has lost a lot of blood.

148
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:37,039
Prepare the hot water.
Prepare the ointments! Come on!

149
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:52,439
Father!

150
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:06,117
Father! My father is
bleeding! My father is dying!

151
00:17:06,118 --> 00:17:09,318
Father, don't die, father!
I am alright, my daughter.

152
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:12,117
My father is dying!
-Ayse... Ayse come.

153
00:17:12,118 --> 00:17:15,079
Come, your father will be alright.
-My father is bleeding.

154
00:17:15,118 --> 00:17:18,358
My father is dying, Fatma
sister! My father is dying!

155
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,919
Alright Ayse, come. Let's go out.

156
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:23,839
Father, don't leave me alone!

157
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:25,710
Don't leave me alone, father!

158
00:17:25,722 --> 00:17:27,519
Don't be afraid, my daughter.

159
00:17:27,598 --> 00:17:30,359
Don't be afraid, I will be alright.
-Ayse, come with me.

160
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,239
Come, they will treat your father. Come on.
-Father...

161
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:36,439
My mother left... Now
you... Don't leave me father!

162
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,279
Father!

163
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,679
Father don't die!
-Ayse, come on!

164
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:44,199
Let's go out, so your father
can recover. Come on.

165
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,099
Father...

166
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,119
Come on.

167
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,479
My knights.

168
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:18,719
Every soldier raised in this
temple will bring hell to the Turks!

169
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,919
Go on

170
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:52,039
My most valuable weapon.

171
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:08,519
That's enough, Poena.

172
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,919
Enough?

173
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:18,679
Do you want me to show
mercy to your soldiers, aunt?

174
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:24,679
Or should I continue with you?

175
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,199
Don't show mercy.

176
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:51,559
The one before you is not me but
Osman, the killer of your parents...

177
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:53,519
...and Bala.

178
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,919
Osman and Bala.

179
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,439
They will both die, aunt.

180
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,279
Osman and Bala.

181
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:23,759
May it be good, God willing.

182
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:31,359
Who are you?

183
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:08,239
My Halime's amulet...

184
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,639
Halime, is that you?

185
00:22:53,070 --> 00:22:54,719
My Halime!

186
00:22:55,931 --> 00:22:57,040
Wait!

187
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:59,879
Wait! Are you here, my daughter?

188
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,919
My Halime!

189
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,079
Is it you, my daughter?

190
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:08,999
Are you here, my daughter? Wait! Don't go!

191
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:19,519
Stop!
Don't leave your mother!

192
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,919
Halime!

193
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,559
Stop!

194
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:34,039
Let me see your face for once!

195
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:36,679
For once, my daughter!

196
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:43,799
Bala!

197
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:48,039
-Mother, are you alright?
-Mother...

198
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,479
Why are you crying? Does it hurt badly?

199
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,559
I am alright.

200
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:57,039
Thanks to Allah.

201
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:05,239
I had a dream...

202
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,679
Dream...

203
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,719
You'll be alright, mother.

204
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:27,999
Is that all the anger you have for
Osman, the killer of your family?

205
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:41,279
You are perfect my little bird.

206
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:59,839
I will take Osman's heart
out with my own hands, aunt.

207
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:02,679
You're amazing, my little bird.

208
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:23,279
My Halime...

209
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:27,159
Let's welcome our guests now, right?

210
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,159
May it be easy Hatuns.

211
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:34,439
Thank you Bala Hatun.
-May it be easy.

212
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:36,039
Welcome to our lands.

213
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:40,519
Come, my beautiful daughter.

214
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:42,959
Let's help them. Come on.

215
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:45,199
Give that to me.

216
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:46,879
Here.

217
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:49,239
Praise be. Praise be.

218
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:52,479
Our Osman Bey is on a conquest.

219
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:56,439
But we brought you his greetings.

220
00:25:56,440 --> 00:25:57,759
Peace be upon him.

221
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:14,239
From now on, our land is your land.

222
00:26:15,080 --> 00:26:17,039
Our food is your food.

223
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,519
Thank you Bala Hatun.

224
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:22,559
You stole my future.

225
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:30,159
And I will wipe out your
lineage with your blood.

226
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:49,079
Come, Halime.

227
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:04,599
-Is the child ready? Everything is ready.

228
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,799
-Do they look alike?
-Yes.

229
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:10,039
We attacked the caravan
heading to the headquarters.

230
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:12,639
The news will arrive soon.

231
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:16,599
We've waited for this day for so long.

232
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:20,999
You know very well what to do.

233
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:25,319
You will distract the cook
and you take the child.

234
00:27:28,160 --> 00:27:30,319
Say goodbye to your daughter, Bala.

235
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:38,719
Come on. Now.

236
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:41,319
Come on.

237
00:27:43,890 --> 00:27:46,719
Come my daughter. Ulgen.

238
00:27:46,720 --> 00:27:48,319
My Bala.

239
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:50,599
How's the food? It's ready, isn't it?

240
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:51,959
Don't worry, Bala.

241
00:27:51,960 --> 00:27:53,799
I cooked enough for everyone.

242
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:56,577
Make sure there's nothing
missing for our guests.

243
00:27:56,589 --> 00:27:57,519
Don't worry.

244
00:27:57,520 --> 00:27:58,759
Alright. -Bala Hatun.

245
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:02,417
Bala Hatun, they attacked the
caravan heading to the headquarters.

246
00:28:02,429 --> 00:28:03,639
What?

247
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,079
Bring the horses! Now!

248
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:08,879
Ulgen, when you're done, go back to Yenisehir.

249
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,879
I entrust my Halime to you, alright?
-Alright, Bala.

250
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:14,919
My daughter, wait for
me, I'll come back, alright?

251
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:18,319
Ulgen, come on

252
00:28:19,680 --> 00:28:21,439
Mother, don't go!

253
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:28,079
My Halime, my beautiful daughter,
I will go but I will come back.

254
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:36,079
Come on, my daughter. Come on.
-My dear...

255
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,799
Bring it here. Here!

256
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,799
Come on!

257
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:49,079
Come on

258
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:54,839
She will come, my dear.

259
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:57,159
Don't worry.

260
00:29:00,310 --> 00:29:01,959
She will come back.

261
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:16,359
You look like you're about to give birth.

262
00:29:16,360 --> 00:29:18,719
How much time is left?

263
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:20,119
His father is at war.

264
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:22,719
I will wait until he returns.

265
00:29:38,040 --> 00:29:39,479
You stir it.
-Alright.

266
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,919
Halime...

267
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:58,079
Ulgen Hatun, help!

268
00:29:58,080 --> 00:29:59,519
Allah

269
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,519
Damn...

270
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:10,199
Stop, you will burn yourself!

271
00:30:18,160 --> 00:30:20,479
Halime.

272
00:30:20,979 --> 00:30:21,979
Hi.

273
00:30:22,080 --> 00:30:24,159
Do you want..

274
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:30,519
Your mother is waiting for you, Halime.

275
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:33,879
She said Halime should
come, yes, Halime should come.

276
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:36,439
She said she'll take you with her.

277
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,159
You will come?

278
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:40,279
My good girl.

279
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:44,239
Good girl. Come. Come.

280
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:54,359
Now you are mine, little demon.

281
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:12,199
Where is my mother?

282
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:16,119
You little demon...

283
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:13,279
You sleep, my daughter...

284
00:32:21,760 --> 00:32:23,679
Throw the shoes by the river.

285
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:29,839
Dress the child in her clothes. Then go and
report that the child fell in the river.

286
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:35,559
Days later...

287
00:32:35,560 --> 00:32:39,039
...when they find the child
they will be sure anyway.

288
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:44,479
Come on.

289
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:30,039
Can I take my revenge now?

290
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:36,319
When the time comes,
you will take your revenge.

291
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:37,759
My beautiful Poena.

292
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:40,759
I live on that dream, aunt.

293
00:33:47,820 --> 00:33:48,959
My little bird.

294
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:58,039
But how much longer do I have to wait, aunt?

295
00:34:00,360 --> 00:34:02,559
I must go now.

296
00:34:03,120 --> 00:34:05,799
You will take good care of my Poena.

297
00:34:11,520 --> 00:34:14,288
I'll come again very soon.

298
00:34:17,590 --> 00:34:18,589
Aunt...

299
00:34:19,480 --> 00:34:23,039
I don't want to wait any
longer. Let me come with you.

300
00:34:23,319 --> 00:34:25,079
You see...

301
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:26,638
I'm ready.

302
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:28,399
I'm strong.

303
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:30,279
I can fight.

304
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:34,239
I want to see the killers of
my family, Osman and Bala...

305
00:34:34,760 --> 00:34:37,159
...my enemies now, aunt.

306
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:40,879
Your greatest strength...

307
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:45,079
...will be your patience, my little bird.

308
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:48,039
That's what we said.

309
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:51,438
Rest well tonight.

310
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:06,519
Tomorrow morning.

311
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,839
Be ready at the castle.

312
00:35:26,430 --> 00:35:27,539
My Bala.

313
00:35:28,280 --> 00:35:30,559
I am alright.

314
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:34,439
Come.

315
00:35:34,630 --> 00:35:36,909
Cerkutay.

316
00:35:37,720 --> 00:35:39,519
My Bey.

317
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:41,479
Increase the precautions.

318
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,599
No one will be around the tribe.

319
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:44,719
As you order, my Bey.

320
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:47,279
How's Ilbay's condition, Turhan?
-He's better.

321
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:50,279
They treated his wound, my
Bey. He's in the healing tent.

322
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:53,239
Okay. Now
I go and see him.

323
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:55,679
Then we will organize the council.

324
00:35:55,680 --> 00:35:57,759
Invite all the Beys.
-Yes my Bey.

325
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,599
Bring some sherbet...
I'm too thirsty...

326
00:36:03,800 --> 00:36:05,799
Orhan.

327
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,719
Ilbay.

328
00:36:18,620 --> 00:36:20,079
My Bey..

329
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:26,639
You are alright, huh?

330
00:36:26,640 --> 00:36:27,959
I am alright, my Bey. I am.

331
00:36:29,390 --> 00:36:31,799
I cauterized my wound in the forest myself.

332
00:36:32,240 --> 00:36:35,119
The healer also took care of me, thank him.

333
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:38,919
The news you risked your life to deliver...

334
00:36:40,480 --> 00:36:42,399
..saved Bala's life. Thank you.

335
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:45,079
Sure, my Bey.

336
00:36:47,920 --> 00:36:50,279
But my Bey...

337
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:53,519
The only thing I learned from those infidels...

338
00:36:53,640 --> 00:36:56,237
...is not just about the
attack on Bala Hatun.

339
00:36:56,249 --> 00:36:57,119
What else?

340
00:36:57,600 --> 00:36:59,879
Karesi Bey.

341
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:02,599
He has advanced his alliance with them...

342
00:37:02,600 --> 00:37:05,399
...to the point of selling
steel to the infidels.

343
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:07,039
What are you saying?

344
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:16,239
Selling steel to the infidels?

345
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:19,639
Selling the essence of the
weapon that hits the hand of a Turk..

346
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:21,959
...to the infidels?

347
00:37:26,390 --> 00:37:28,079
Karesi Bey.

348
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:31,039
Your hostility towards us...

349
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:33,279
...has made you this low, huh?

350
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:36,919
My Bey, we must do
whatever it takes to stop this.

351
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:39,999
We will.

352
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:42,239
Of course, we will.

353
00:37:42,680 --> 00:37:44,159
Those Sofia's snakes...

354
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,839
Do they stay in Akhisar Castle?
-My Bey...

355
00:37:49,200 --> 00:37:51,359
..from what I heard from Sofia's men...

356
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:52,999
...they hide in a temple.

357
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,439
Where is this temple?

358
00:37:55,440 --> 00:37:57,759
I could not learn that, my Bey.

359
00:37:57,760 --> 00:38:01,679
But the horses of those men who
came to the castle were never tired.

360
00:38:01,840 --> 00:38:04,679
It seems the place is not far from Akhisar.

361
00:38:05,760 --> 00:38:08,439
Orhan. -My Bey. -Tomorrow...

362
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:11,679
You will observe all the
temples around Akhisar.

363
00:38:11,960 --> 00:38:15,079
You will find out where Sofia's snakes are.

364
00:38:15,080 --> 00:38:17,279
As you say, my Bey.

365
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:22,799
Since you are well...

366
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:26,039
...regain your strength. From now on...

367
00:38:27,320 --> 00:38:29,199
...you will stay with us.

368
00:38:30,720 --> 00:38:33,039
As you say, my Bey.

369
00:38:50,720 --> 00:38:53,599
You have nine lives, Lukas.

370
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:59,079
You survived Osman's clutches again.

371
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:03,439
He survived, not me.

372
00:39:03,880 --> 00:39:07,679
If he hadn't arrived just in
time, we'd have killed his wife.

373
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:10,319
But she turned out to be lucky.

374
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:14,359
We shouldn't mess with
women and children, Lukas.

375
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:17,679
I want war and blood.

376
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:22,319
I will disgrace Osman on the battlefield.

377
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:26,279
We will, Karesi Bey.

378
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:28,559
Together, we will.

379
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:30,679
As I said before,

380
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:35,719
...my army needs steel. Osman
destroyed my mine, you know.

381
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:37,839
Is everything ready?

382
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:40,639
Yes, yes.

383
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:46,199
I got it brought from the castle of
Karadin that Osman gave to me.

384
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:50,759
We'll hit him with his own weapon, huh?

385
00:39:51,920 --> 00:39:54,399
I already hit him.

386
00:39:55,080 --> 00:39:58,679
I put a snake inside Osman's tent.

387
00:39:58,840 --> 00:40:01,119
It is such a snake that...

388
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:06,959
...it will let me know about
Osman's every step and breath.

389
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:13,119
You got one of his beys, huh?

390
00:40:13,760 --> 00:40:16,519
Yes, yes.

391
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:23,399
But I have one more person
that I've wanted to get for so long.

392
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:26,119
Someone precious.

393
00:40:26,560 --> 00:40:31,479
And I don't want her to
be hurt when the war starts.

394
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:33,559
Who?

395
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,839
Which one?

396
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:50,159
Lukas.

397
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:54,239
And Karesi Bey who collaborates with him.

398
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:56,239
And..

399
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:59,079
The demon called Sofia...

400
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:03,119
...who came across me again.

401
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:08,439
The number of our enemies
is increasing day by day.

402
00:41:08,680 --> 00:41:11,319
We have three fronts at war.

403
00:41:11,760 --> 00:41:19,999
While there are so many heathens who want
to break our claws and disgrace our state,

404
00:41:21,400 --> 00:41:22,599
...Muslims should never..

405
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:26,399
...ever make any mistakes.

406
00:41:27,640 --> 00:41:28,679
You should...

407
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:31,159
...know that well.

408
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:38,479
We will stay in our land in peace and order.

409
00:41:39,120 --> 00:41:42,039
So everybody should do...

410
00:41:42,760 --> 00:41:46,439
...their duties with more care.

411
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:48,959
Now tell me.

412
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:50,919
Begum Hatun.

413
00:41:51,240 --> 00:41:54,479
What's the condition of the
merchants and local people?

414
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:59,599
Does anyone have a problem?

415
00:42:00,040 --> 00:42:02,239
They have no problems, my Bey.

416
00:42:02,440 --> 00:42:06,359
Merchants are pleased to trade in our market.

417
00:42:07,200 --> 00:42:09,879
Okay, okay.

418
00:42:12,920 --> 00:42:14,479
You tell me, Gencer Bey.

419
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:17,039
What's the situation in Mekece?

420
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:18,919
Are your alps...

421
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:21,319
...cautious?

422
00:42:21,560 --> 00:42:23,639
We took all the measures, my Bey.

423
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:26,479
The castle is safe, for sure.

424
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,879
But...

425
00:42:29,081 --> 00:42:31,320
I don't understand one thing, Osman Bey.

426
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:34,799
Someone told Karesi Bey about our hunting plan.

427
00:42:36,760 --> 00:42:39,519
I thought you'd bring up the subject, but...

428
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:43,639
...we're talking about the market and Mekece.

429
00:42:44,080 --> 00:42:46,959
This council is the secret center of the state.

430
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:51,719
If there is someone you suspect among us,

431
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:54,119
...expose him right here right now.

432
00:42:54,400 --> 00:43:00,319
Otherwise, none of us can stand
with our heads up before you.

433
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:03,879
Gencer Bey is right, my Bey.

434
00:43:04,680 --> 00:43:07,999
Even if there is little suspicion,

435
00:43:08,200 --> 00:43:12,119
...we should arrest the
traitor and have a trial.

436
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:26,519
I talked to Karesi...

437
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:32,639
...just to bait him.

438
00:43:35,040 --> 00:43:40,759
If he were working with a traitor among us

439
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:48,359
...he would have shown his true color.

440
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:58,239
Well... It seems he found out
about the hunting plan by observing.

441
00:44:02,160 --> 00:44:03,999
You should know this.

442
00:44:05,280 --> 00:44:12,959
I fully trust my beys in the
council and my alps in the army!

443
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:23,479
Otherwise...

444
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:27,959
Otherwise...

445
00:44:28,880 --> 00:44:33,199
...we wouldn't be talking
about the state affairs here.

446
00:44:37,240 --> 00:44:44,319
From now on, while performing their duties,

447
00:44:45,280 --> 00:44:49,879
...everybody will be more careful and cautious.

448
00:44:58,200 --> 00:44:59,719
You may leave.

449
00:45:11,680 --> 00:45:14,239
One of them is betraying us.

450
00:45:16,600 --> 00:45:18,919
We will find out who.

451
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:27,279
We will talk about that now.

452
00:45:34,800 --> 00:45:38,679
One of the merchants left this
saying it's important, Begum Hatun.

453
00:45:48,280 --> 00:45:51,759
He's looking for a traitor even in his shadow.

454
00:45:52,160 --> 00:45:54,999
And you send me a message to meet?

455
00:45:55,680 --> 00:45:57,799
I know what to do.

456
00:45:58,600 --> 00:46:00,599
Prepare my horse.

457
00:46:05,280 --> 00:46:09,519
You said you fully trust them in the council.

458
00:46:09,640 --> 00:46:13,119
You did that to clear their
suspicion, huh, my Bey?

459
00:46:13,640 --> 00:46:16,039
Yes. Yes.

460
00:46:16,680 --> 00:46:18,479
Well..

461
00:46:18,920 --> 00:46:23,279
Being a state is something like this.

462
00:46:25,040 --> 00:46:28,479
Begum, Bayhan or Gencer.

463
00:46:30,280 --> 00:46:36,359
One of them betrayed us and the state.

464
00:46:41,400 --> 00:46:45,359
Whoever is that vile dog,

465
00:46:46,560 --> 00:46:50,759
...we will find evidence and expose.

466
00:46:51,080 --> 00:46:53,719
And we will punish.

467
00:46:55,840 --> 00:46:58,679
Boran. Cerkutay. This is my order.
-My Bey.

468
00:46:59,120 --> 00:47:03,119
You'll always keep your eyes on them.

469
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:08,759
You will tell me about every step they take.

470
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:11,439
As you order, my Bey.

471
00:47:23,200 --> 00:47:28,319
The jackal who eats the council
up and exposes the state's secrets...

472
00:47:28,360 --> 00:47:30,599
...will be revealed soon, brother.

473
00:47:32,680 --> 00:47:34,079
Brother.

474
00:47:34,880 --> 00:47:37,239
The traitor in the council...

475
00:47:39,440 --> 00:47:41,839
...is Begum Hatun. I'm sure of that.

476
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:46,039
She made mistakes over and over again.

477
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:49,359
I have the same name in my mind.

478
00:48:01,040 --> 00:48:03,119
Where do you think she's going?

479
00:48:04,240 --> 00:48:06,999
-To Karesi?
-We'll find out.

480
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:09,199
Let's go.
Let's go.

481
00:48:12,040 --> 00:48:18,599
While Orhan is looking for the dog's nest,
the temple where Sofia's soldiers hide in,

482
00:48:19,960 --> 00:48:24,468
...we will land our punch
at Karesi Bey who sells

483
00:48:25,340 --> 00:48:28,999
steel to heathens and
forgets he's a Turk himself.

484
00:48:32,560 --> 00:48:35,199
We'll hit him where he betrays.

485
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:41,399
We'll hit him with the steel
that he sends to the heathens.

486
00:49:00,240 --> 00:49:05,319
This is the moment of truth, brother.

487
00:50:07,120 --> 00:50:09,679
That's Karesi coming.

488
00:50:16,360 --> 00:50:20,279
Traitor! Vile traitor.

489
00:50:20,800 --> 00:50:24,359
We always get in trouble
as we have a traitor inside.

490
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:28,959
-The punishment will be so harsh.
-It will be.

491
00:50:29,280 --> 00:50:31,239
It will be.

492
00:50:33,360 --> 00:50:36,479
Welcome, Begum Hatun.

493
00:50:36,720 --> 00:50:38,799
I'm not welcome, Karesi Bey.

494
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:41,599
I have things to tell you.

495
00:50:43,320 --> 00:50:47,479
But first you tell me why you invited me.

496
00:50:48,440 --> 00:50:53,759
I want to save you from the flames of the fire.

497
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:57,479
I invited you for this, Begum Hatun.

498
00:50:59,320 --> 00:51:02,719
I've managed on my own so far.

499
00:51:03,720 --> 00:51:06,399
So I expect help from nobody.

500
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:11,359
Don't contact me again, Karesi Bey.

501
00:51:11,640 --> 00:51:16,639
Well... You asked me to pledge loyalty to you.

502
00:51:17,200 --> 00:51:21,119
You keep sending notes
and gifts. But it's enough.

503
00:51:26,080 --> 00:51:33,039
You asked me to wear this
necklace when I offer my loyalty.

504
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:37,199
But I won't offer my loyalty to you.

505
00:51:39,120 --> 00:51:42,759
Don't come to me with such an offer again.

506
00:51:47,720 --> 00:51:51,719
I care about your life, Begum Hatun.

507
00:51:52,320 --> 00:51:54,319
You're on the wrong side.

508
00:51:54,720 --> 00:51:56,159
But..

509
00:51:56,640 --> 00:51:58,279
It's your choice.

510
00:52:00,520 --> 00:52:03,159
Keep the necklace as a memory.

511
00:52:04,240 --> 00:52:06,919
I understand you.

512
00:52:08,840 --> 00:52:10,839
Stay safe.

513
00:53:01,360 --> 00:53:03,119
What's going on here?

514
00:53:03,600 --> 00:53:05,479
Ulgen!

515
00:53:07,280 --> 00:53:08,839
Ulgen!

516
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:12,239
Ulgen, what's going on here?

517
00:53:15,520 --> 00:53:17,159
Ulgen?

518
00:53:17,400 --> 00:53:19,799
I couldn't protect.

519
00:53:21,840 --> 00:53:24,319
Protect what?
-I couldn't.

520
00:53:24,520 --> 00:53:27,119
I couldn't.

521
00:53:27,720 --> 00:53:31,479
Ulgen, where is Halime? Where is Halime?

522
00:53:31,760 --> 00:53:34,039
-She fell.
-Where is she?

523
00:53:34,040 --> 00:53:36,159
I couldn't find her.

524
00:53:36,320 --> 00:53:37,959
Search everywhere!

525
00:53:38,040 --> 00:53:39,999
Halime! Halime!

526
00:53:41,240 --> 00:53:43,279
My daughter!

527
00:53:43,520 --> 00:53:47,439
My dear... Search
everywhere! Search everywhere!

528
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:52,479
Search everywhere!

529
00:53:56,640 --> 00:53:58,479
Halime!

530
00:53:59,360 --> 00:54:02,719
No! Halime!

531
00:54:02,920 --> 00:54:07,959
No! Halime! My dear!

532
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:12,079
My dear!

533
00:54:39,800 --> 00:54:40,519
Halime.

534
00:54:46,280 --> 00:54:48,119
My beautiful daughter.

535
00:54:57,280 --> 00:54:58,999
Bala.

536
00:55:04,960 --> 00:55:06,559
What's going on?

537
00:55:20,120 --> 00:55:23,999
Your wound is opened again.
Your heart is hurting, right?

538
00:55:26,920 --> 00:55:28,959
This pain never ends.

539
00:55:30,160 --> 00:55:35,799
That's why I can't say anything
about Gonca's suffering.

540
00:55:36,360 --> 00:55:38,879
No words could fit.

541
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:43,679
I can't say her grief would end.

542
00:55:48,160 --> 00:55:51,559
Don't cry inside. Come to me.

543
00:55:51,760 --> 00:55:53,879
Come to me.

544
00:55:57,880 --> 00:56:01,559
Here, you can cry as much as you want.

545
00:56:03,960 --> 00:56:06,479
You had the same dream again?

546
00:56:07,560 --> 00:56:09,999
I saw Halime again.

547
00:56:11,800 --> 00:56:13,879
She's grown up.

548
00:56:14,200 --> 00:56:16,839
With her silky long hair.

549
00:56:18,800 --> 00:56:22,279
I ran after her but I couldn't arrive in time.

550
00:56:23,360 --> 00:56:28,359
I couldn't see her face.
-Close your eyes.

551
00:56:31,360 --> 00:56:35,639
Her eyes are just like yours.

552
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:44,159
Her hair is long just like yours.

553
00:56:46,080 --> 00:56:50,239
She takes after her mother.

554
00:56:53,760 --> 00:56:55,079
Osman.

555
00:56:57,400 --> 00:57:00,079
Sofia told me such a thing...

556
00:57:00,400 --> 00:57:03,119
...that I can't help
thinking about it.

557
00:57:04,440 --> 00:57:05,799
What did she say?

558
00:57:06,000 --> 00:57:09,919
"I'll tell you such a
thing without killing you...

559
00:57:10,240 --> 00:57:13,239
...that you'll beg me to live", she said.

560
00:57:14,200 --> 00:57:16,839
Sofia knows both of us well.

561
00:57:17,400 --> 00:57:20,119
She knows we won't bow against her.

562
00:57:22,120 --> 00:57:24,199
What can be...

563
00:57:25,680 --> 00:57:28,919
...the secret which can
make us bow against her?

564
00:57:42,560 --> 00:57:44,199
My almighty God.

565
00:57:44,680 --> 00:57:48,289
I'm begging you to let me
take revenge on those...

566
00:57:48,301 --> 00:57:51,559
...evil Turks who stole
my family and childhood.

567
00:57:53,440 --> 00:58:01,519
Give me strength to kill Osman,
Bala, their children, all of them.

568
00:58:02,640 --> 00:58:05,639
My suffering can be relieved only in this way.

569
00:58:05,720 --> 00:58:08,239
This great hole inside me...

570
00:58:09,360 --> 00:58:12,039
...will be filled as they bleed.

571
00:58:12,480 --> 00:58:14,399
Amen.

572
00:58:24,120 --> 00:58:30,439
With a tiny piece of information, Karesi
Bey made Osman a prey during his own hunt.

573
00:58:32,600 --> 00:58:39,119
Who knows what he can do to him when
he learns about Osman's new decisions?

574
00:58:55,080 --> 00:58:57,089
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

575
00:58:57,089 --> 00:58:58,919
Aykurt, Is our Bey in his tent?

576
00:58:58,920 --> 00:59:00,519
Yes, Boran Bey.

577
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:03,999
Brother, hold these.

578
00:59:05,080 --> 00:59:07,519
Thanks. Come on.

579
00:59:14,280 --> 00:59:16,079
Do I have permission, my Bey?

580
00:59:16,480 --> 00:59:18,119
Come in.

581
00:59:20,840 --> 00:59:23,279
-My Bey.
-Are there any updates?

582
00:59:23,480 --> 00:59:26,039
Begum Hatun and Karesi Bey met, my Bey.

583
00:59:26,760 --> 00:59:30,719
It seems they've been
communicating for a long time, my Bey.

584
00:59:33,120 --> 00:59:36,799
You say so? Where is she now?
-On the way, my Bey.

585
00:59:37,080 --> 00:59:38,919
She'll arrive soon.

586
00:59:40,960 --> 00:59:42,799
What did they talk about?

587
00:59:43,160 --> 00:59:45,719
That's the main concern, my Bey.

588
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:54,879
Where have you been, sister?
You left without telling anyone.

589
00:59:55,200 --> 00:59:56,719
What's the matter?

590
00:59:56,840 --> 00:59:59,119
Are you questioning your sister now?

591
00:59:59,440 --> 01:00:01,759
You should have told me at least.

592
01:00:03,040 --> 01:00:06,359
I'd have told you if you
had needed to know, brother.

593
01:00:09,800 --> 01:00:13,679
-Hey!
-What is this, Aykurt Cavus?

594
01:00:14,480 --> 01:00:17,359
We're here with Osman
Bey's orders, Begum Hatun.

595
01:00:17,480 --> 01:00:21,719
Your betrayal to the state and
Osman Bey has been exposed.

596
01:00:26,320 --> 01:00:28,839
It's time for punishment.

597
01:00:30,080 --> 01:00:32,679
Sisters! Alps! Take her.

598
01:00:32,840 --> 01:00:35,439
-You're making a mistake.
-Aykurt Cavus!

599
01:00:36,160 --> 01:00:38,479
This is Osman Bey's order.

600
01:00:38,840 --> 01:00:41,639
Raise no difficulties. Come on.

601
01:00:44,680 --> 01:00:47,919
I didn't betray Osman Bey! I didn't!

602
01:00:55,520 --> 01:00:57,399
It's foggy.

603
01:00:57,920 --> 01:01:01,799
We'll go there and be back quickly
without drawing any suspicion.

604
01:01:02,720 --> 01:01:05,759
Where are you going so late, Gencer Bey?

605
01:01:10,160 --> 01:01:12,759
What is this at this hour, my Bey?

606
01:01:15,720 --> 01:01:16,919
O people

607
01:01:17,120 --> 01:01:18,799
Osman Bey's orders!

608
01:01:19,080 --> 01:01:20,999
Everybody gather in the square!

609
01:01:22,320 --> 01:01:26,199
Shortly we will know if it's good or not.

610
01:01:44,040 --> 01:01:48,719
Obviously, something big will
happen at this late hour of the night.

611
01:01:48,960 --> 01:01:51,759
Attention! Osman Bey!

612
01:02:14,320 --> 01:02:16,279
O people!

613
01:02:18,200 --> 01:02:23,319
My house, my beys and sisters...

614
01:02:23,800 --> 01:02:27,959
We've been looking for a traitor in
the council and tribe for a long time.

615
01:02:29,600 --> 01:02:31,239
And now...

616
01:02:32,440 --> 01:02:35,319
And now we know who the traitor is.

617
01:02:38,280 --> 01:02:42,559
The traitor who looks like one of
us, tells the enemy our secrets...

618
01:02:43,400 --> 01:02:48,599
...and collaborates with
Karesi Bey behind my back...

619
01:02:55,160 --> 01:02:57,199
...is Begum Hatun.

620
01:03:02,120 --> 01:03:04,319
Bring her.

621
01:03:23,240 --> 01:03:25,479
You will be tried Begum Hatun.

622
01:03:25,480 --> 01:03:27,999
Osman Bey, I...
Search her clothes.

623
01:03:54,800 --> 01:04:01,279
A pearl necklace, a pearl necklace.

624
01:04:05,480 --> 01:04:07,719
That really suits Karesi Bey.

625
01:04:14,800 --> 01:04:17,319
Did Karesi Bey gift this to you?
-Yes, my Bey, but...

626
01:04:17,320 --> 01:04:18,879
My Osman Bey...

627
01:04:18,880 --> 01:04:21,199
...my sister would never betray you.

628
01:04:21,200 --> 01:04:23,599
Let her explain herself. -No.

629
01:04:26,560 --> 01:04:27,599
Cerkutay Bey...

630
01:04:28,120 --> 01:04:30,519
...and Boran Bey...

631
01:04:31,920 --> 01:04:33,879
...saw and heard everything...

632
01:04:34,920 --> 01:04:37,079
...while watching Begum Hatun.

633
01:04:41,680 --> 01:04:43,799
The evidence of betrayal..

634
01:04:44,520 --> 01:04:47,679
...is this pearl necklace gifted by Karesi Bey.

635
01:04:47,680 --> 01:04:49,519
My Bey, that's not how it happened. -No!

636
01:04:50,560 --> 01:04:52,719
Enough

637
01:04:52,720 --> 01:04:54,559
Betrayal cannot be explained.

638
01:05:01,800 --> 01:05:04,439
You will stand trial...

639
01:05:04,440 --> 01:05:06,519
...and be judged.

640
01:05:13,040 --> 01:05:15,079
Yusuf Bey...

641
01:05:15,080 --> 01:05:17,959
...we will investigate whether you are...

642
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:20,039
...involved in this.

643
01:05:21,920 --> 01:05:24,519
Until Begum Hatun stands trial...

644
01:05:25,320 --> 01:05:27,719
...you will be under watch in the tribe.

645
01:05:30,960 --> 01:05:33,239
Take her to the caged tent.

646
01:05:35,800 --> 01:05:37,679
Sister.

647
01:05:47,000 --> 01:05:48,919
Come on.

648
01:05:52,360 --> 01:05:55,519
Finally, Begum Hatun's
true face has been revealed.

649
01:05:57,800 --> 01:06:00,479
I think Yusuf is also involved in this.

650
01:06:01,170 --> 01:06:03,479
Being under watch is not enough for him.

651
01:06:08,400 --> 01:06:11,639
Now, even if Yusuf catches
a bird with his mouth...

652
01:06:11,640 --> 01:06:14,439
...he won't be able to
get close to Fatma Hatun.

653
01:06:14,920 --> 01:06:17,319
Use this situation well, my son.

654
01:06:17,800 --> 01:06:19,879
Come on.

655
01:06:24,920 --> 01:06:27,479
Come here, Gunkurt.

656
01:06:28,200 --> 01:06:30,679
Osman must have sent his Alps after me.

657
01:06:30,920 --> 01:06:32,119
I cannot leave now.

658
01:06:34,200 --> 01:06:36,079
Go to Karesi and tell him.

659
01:06:37,120 --> 01:06:39,919
Tell him Begum Hatun was caught. But...

660
01:06:40,720 --> 01:06:43,239
Be careful... Alright? Go.

661
01:06:43,240 --> 01:06:45,759
Yes my Bey.

662
01:06:50,120 --> 01:06:51,279
Get ready!

663
01:06:52,840 --> 01:06:54,199
My Bey..

664
01:06:54,560 --> 01:06:55,439
Wait!

665
01:06:57,080 --> 01:06:58,639
I'll come with you

666
01:07:00,720 --> 01:07:02,039
Father!

667
01:07:05,600 --> 01:07:09,559
I told you to get well soon but I
didn't think it would be this soon.

668
01:07:09,640 --> 01:07:11,919
Resting does not suit a Turk, my Bey.

669
01:07:12,120 --> 01:07:14,559
Even if I stay, my blood will boil inside me.

670
01:07:14,560 --> 01:07:15,959
Fair enough.

671
01:07:15,960 --> 01:07:17,079
My dear.

672
01:07:18,320 --> 01:07:20,879
Come on, to horses!

673
01:07:27,440 --> 01:07:29,399
May your fight bring victory, Bey.

674
01:07:29,400 --> 01:07:31,319
Thank you Bala, thank you.

675
01:07:44,360 --> 01:07:47,079
Come on, let's go to the Sogut marketplace.

676
01:07:47,200 --> 01:07:50,359
Mother, can I come to
the Sogut marketplace too?

677
01:07:50,880 --> 01:07:51,959
I get bored here.

678
01:07:52,480 --> 01:07:54,919
Besides, you'll be with me there.

679
01:07:55,800 --> 01:07:57,559
Alright. Come.

680
01:07:57,560 --> 01:08:00,119
But you will not leave my side for a second!

681
01:08:00,640 --> 01:08:02,359
Where is Gonca?

682
01:08:02,360 --> 01:08:03,999
I don't know.

683
01:08:04,000 --> 01:08:07,359
Call her now, we have
to go. Let's not waste time.

684
01:08:07,800 --> 01:08:09,239
You go and bring her.

685
01:08:09,400 --> 01:08:10,519
Come on.

686
01:08:19,350 --> 01:08:21,719
Gonca Hatun.

687
01:08:27,709 --> 01:08:29,599
Get out.

688
01:08:31,520 --> 01:08:34,839
I have things to talk about with Begum Hatun.

689
01:08:42,560 --> 01:08:45,399
-Do you also believe I am a traitor?
-Aren't you?

690
01:08:46,640 --> 01:08:49,037
Don't, Gonca..

691
01:08:49,040 --> 01:08:51,319
Why would I betray Osman Bey?

692
01:08:51,319 --> 01:08:53,479
I believe you.

693
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:56,719
You would not betray my father.

694
01:08:58,960 --> 01:09:01,399
Because you love him, Begum Hatun.

695
01:09:03,240 --> 01:09:05,278
Gonca Hatun.

696
01:09:05,279 --> 01:09:06,759
What...

697
01:09:06,760 --> 01:09:09,559
What are you saying?

698
01:09:10,319 --> 01:09:12,198
It's not true...

699
01:09:12,200 --> 01:09:15,439
-Whoever said it..
Will you call it a lie now, Begum?

700
01:09:17,720 --> 01:09:20,599
I heard it from you, not someone else.

701
01:09:27,560 --> 01:09:28,999
Don't...

702
01:09:29,600 --> 01:09:30,799
Don't tell anyone..

703
01:09:31,200 --> 01:09:33,759
What you're doing is very wrong.

704
01:09:35,160 --> 01:09:36,037
But...

705
01:09:38,880 --> 01:09:42,639
...staying here while
you are innocent is unfair.

706
01:09:43,560 --> 01:09:45,799
Therefore, I will talk to my mother and father.

707
01:09:45,800 --> 01:09:47,359
I will tell them everything.

708
01:09:47,679 --> 01:09:49,299
Gonca..

709
01:09:50,160 --> 01:09:54,078
If you tell something to someone...

710
01:09:55,000 --> 01:09:57,719
...I won't be able to
look at their faces again.

711
01:10:00,680 --> 01:10:02,759
It's time, Hatun.

712
01:10:05,140 --> 01:10:08,679
Bala Hatun and the others will
soon leave to go to the marketplace.

713
01:10:08,800 --> 01:10:09,879
Good.

714
01:10:13,080 --> 01:10:15,239
Come on Gulce.

715
01:10:17,040 --> 01:10:19,759
Please, Gonca, listen to me and don't do it!

716
01:10:50,194 --> 01:10:52,504
Akhisar Castle

717
01:10:54,000 --> 01:10:57,119
Karesi's steel caravan will be here shortly.

718
01:10:57,640 --> 01:11:00,279
This will be the biggest and...

719
01:11:01,160 --> 01:11:03,559
...grandest agreement of Byzantium.

720
01:11:03,560 --> 01:11:06,799
Sofia.
-Stop.

721
01:11:08,920 --> 01:11:13,679
Karesi is giving the Turks' most
valuable treasure to their eternal enemies.

722
01:11:16,090 --> 01:11:18,209
Lukas...

723
01:11:19,960 --> 01:11:23,159
With this agreement, history will be rewritten.

724
01:11:24,920 --> 01:11:26,959
Imagine...

725
01:11:27,840 --> 01:11:32,799
The miraculous steel that strengthens the
Turks' swords and brings them victories...

726
01:11:32,800 --> 01:11:35,039
...will become a merciless weapon..

727
01:11:35,280 --> 01:11:37,239
...in the hands of...

728
01:11:37,760 --> 01:11:39,639
...Byzantine blacksmiths.

729
01:11:41,280 --> 01:11:44,639
Once those weapons come
together with my own weapon...

730
01:11:47,920 --> 01:11:50,679
...we will become the Turks' nightmare, Lukas.

731
01:11:56,760 --> 01:11:58,359
That secret...

732
01:11:59,200 --> 01:12:00,199
Sofia...

733
01:12:02,900 --> 01:12:05,159
Aren't you really going to tell me?

734
01:12:05,160 --> 01:12:07,959
Osman and Bala's daughter.

735
01:12:10,120 --> 01:12:11,999
I have her.

736
01:12:17,280 --> 01:12:20,519
Halime, whom everyone thought was dead.

737
01:12:28,360 --> 01:12:30,239
Halime.

738
01:12:31,540 --> 01:12:33,439
Halime...

739
01:12:34,480 --> 01:12:37,319
...is my niece Poena, Lukas.

740
01:12:41,760 --> 01:12:42,799
How?

741
01:12:45,200 --> 01:12:49,519
I kidnapped her years ago and
convinced them that she was dead.

742
01:12:52,920 --> 01:12:57,639
Bala has been crying at the grave of
a girl she never knew for years.

743
01:13:01,320 --> 01:13:05,199
Did you turn Osman's own
daughter against her family?

744
01:13:10,520 --> 01:13:14,439
You are the devil itself, Sofia.

745
01:13:21,560 --> 01:13:22,839
Aunt.

746
01:13:38,000 --> 01:13:41,119
Welcome, my little bird.

747
01:13:46,280 --> 01:13:49,079
Meet Commander Lukas.

748
01:13:49,600 --> 01:13:51,799
I am glad to meet you Poena.

749
01:13:52,320 --> 01:13:55,799
It's an honour to meet you Commander Lukas.

750
01:13:55,800 --> 01:13:59,119
That honour belongs to me.

751
01:14:05,030 --> 01:14:07,519
The day you waited for has come.

752
01:14:09,040 --> 01:14:12,399
You will go to Sogut...

753
01:14:12,400 --> 01:14:15,199
...to meet your enemies.

754
01:14:50,000 --> 01:14:50,999
Boran.

755
01:14:51,800 --> 01:14:52,399
Yes?

756
01:14:53,200 --> 01:14:54,479
Brother.

757
01:14:56,280 --> 01:14:57,959
Did we not become a state?

758
01:14:59,320 --> 01:15:00,959
We did, brother.

759
01:15:02,480 --> 01:15:04,959
Why does my Bey come to every battle with us?

760
01:15:04,960 --> 01:15:07,599
Could we not have raided this place ourselves?

761
01:15:07,640 --> 01:15:10,359
Why did he not sit on
his chair and give orders?

762
01:15:10,440 --> 01:15:14,919
But no... -Brother...

763
01:15:15,040 --> 01:15:17,759
Look, state matters do not work like that.

764
01:15:17,760 --> 01:15:19,079
You know the state matters, brother.

765
01:15:19,080 --> 01:15:20,239
Brother, let me answer.

766
01:15:20,240 --> 01:15:21,439
Did you understand what I said?

767
01:15:21,440 --> 01:15:24,120
How do state matters work
then? You always know everything!

768
01:15:24,132 --> 01:15:25,119
Cerkutay, brother...

769
01:15:25,120 --> 01:15:27,119
What is going on there?

770
01:15:28,880 --> 01:15:31,119
What are you whispering about?

771
01:15:31,440 --> 01:15:33,799
Come on, say it so we can hear it.

772
01:15:39,040 --> 01:15:40,519
My Bey.

773
01:15:45,920 --> 01:15:49,649
Boran is asking why our Bey
comes with us to every battle.

774
01:15:54,240 --> 01:15:57,479
He says we could have
raided this place ourselves.

775
01:15:57,480 --> 01:16:00,919
He says you could have just sat
on your chair and given orders.

776
01:16:00,960 --> 01:16:03,279
I also do not understand why he says that.

777
01:16:03,280 --> 01:16:06,119
What are you saying, you mad man?

778
01:16:10,320 --> 01:16:11,559
So Boran says that, huh?

779
01:16:13,560 --> 01:16:14,799
Yes, my Bey.

780
01:16:14,880 --> 01:16:18,089
Boran says that, but you
know he sometimes is not sane.

781
01:16:18,800 --> 01:16:21,439
Then tell Boran to listen carefully.

782
01:16:24,240 --> 01:16:29,029
A horse of the man whose Bey
does not run ahead will never run.

783
01:16:31,520 --> 01:16:34,806
The state of a Bey who only
gives orders from his chair

784
01:16:34,818 --> 01:16:37,999
and does not go to battle
will certainly be powerless.

785
01:16:38,320 --> 01:16:43,999
Whether we are Beys or Sultans, we will
never forget why we came to this world.

786
01:16:46,400 --> 01:16:49,999
It is our duty to fight the
infidels on the battlefield.

787
01:16:50,120 --> 01:16:51,999
Yes my Bey.

788
01:16:58,160 --> 01:16:59,479
Aykurt.

789
01:17:00,040 --> 01:17:02,199
My Bey, the caravan is approaching.

790
01:17:02,360 --> 01:17:04,759
Let them come.

791
01:17:06,280 --> 01:17:08,119
We will not harm the Alps.

792
01:17:08,120 --> 01:17:10,519
You will arrest all of them.

793
01:17:11,280 --> 01:17:13,399
Yes my Bey.

794
01:17:13,400 --> 01:17:15,719
Come on Alps!

795
01:17:15,720 --> 01:17:17,959
Come on

796
01:17:55,470 --> 01:17:57,559
What is happening here?

797
01:18:07,680 --> 01:18:09,039
Alps!

798
01:18:09,040 --> 01:18:10,559
Attack!

799
01:18:10,560 --> 01:18:12,919
Ya Allah

800
01:18:36,680 --> 01:18:39,039
Kneel

801
01:18:51,840 --> 01:18:53,999
What is happening?

802
01:18:54,000 --> 01:18:56,599
You will pay for this!

803
01:18:57,840 --> 01:19:00,959
We are the ones who will make...

804
01:19:02,200 --> 01:19:04,159
...others pay, Sancar. Know that.

805
01:19:05,680 --> 01:19:08,799
The price for working with traitors is death...

806
01:19:08,920 --> 01:19:11,239
...but you should thank Osman Bey.

807
01:19:31,000 --> 01:19:34,879
My Bey, the caravan is filled with mine!

808
01:19:39,720 --> 01:19:41,879
What does this mean, Osman Bey?

809
01:19:42,560 --> 01:19:45,519
Raiding the caravan of Karesi Bey...

810
01:19:45,560 --> 01:19:48,639
Do you think you can get away with this?

811
01:19:48,640 --> 01:19:51,879
You sold the mine that would
be swords for the Alps, huh?

812
01:19:52,880 --> 01:19:55,839
You will have no place
to rest in either world.

813
01:19:56,160 --> 01:19:58,839
Are we going to ask you what to sell to whom?

814
01:19:59,160 --> 01:20:02,119
How can you even question Karesi Bey, Osman?

815
01:20:02,120 --> 01:20:02,999
Shut up

816
01:20:03,560 --> 01:20:05,039
What are you saying?

817
01:20:05,080 --> 01:20:07,119
Hear your own words!

818
01:20:07,120 --> 01:20:09,519
You are talking to Osman Bey!

819
01:20:17,280 --> 01:20:19,719
Where is your Bey?

820
01:20:19,720 --> 01:20:22,319
Why can't I see him?

821
01:20:22,680 --> 01:20:25,435
You don't even see
how small you are but you

822
01:20:25,447 --> 01:20:28,399
raid our caravan, and
then you ask me questions.

823
01:20:30,390 --> 01:20:32,499
What do you think you are doing?

824
01:20:34,790 --> 01:20:36,719
Here...

825
01:20:36,720 --> 01:20:39,359
I am the Bey, and I am the state.

826
01:20:45,800 --> 01:20:48,319
I do not ask questions.

827
01:20:48,320 --> 01:20:51,039
I call everyone to account.

828
01:21:16,480 --> 01:21:17,439
Now..

829
01:21:18,360 --> 01:21:20,639
Go and tell your Bey.

830
01:21:21,320 --> 01:21:24,599
I have his spy Begum Hatun.

831
01:21:24,600 --> 01:21:27,199
Now, this caravan is mine.

832
01:21:27,200 --> 01:21:28,879
Come on now.

833
01:21:28,880 --> 01:21:32,159
Go and tell him that Osman Bey started the war.

834
01:21:37,360 --> 01:21:38,399
Now..

835
01:21:38,920 --> 01:21:40,959
Start running away...

836
01:21:40,960 --> 01:21:44,439
...and tell your Bey what you saw. Go now!

837
01:21:48,600 --> 01:21:49,839
Alaeddin. -My Bey.

838
01:21:50,520 --> 01:21:52,839
Be careful.

839
01:21:53,240 --> 01:21:54,519
The fuse is lit now.

840
01:21:56,680 --> 01:21:58,839
From now on, the war will begin.

841
01:21:59,880 --> 01:22:01,479
-Yes my Bey.
-Come on!

842
01:22:16,320 --> 01:22:19,079
They are close. They are coming.

843
01:22:47,000 --> 01:22:48,399
Oghuz. -My Bey.

844
01:22:58,120 --> 01:23:01,399
We have reached the
frontiers that Ilbay mentioned.

845
01:23:01,600 --> 01:23:04,239
But we could not see anything.

846
01:23:05,360 --> 01:23:08,359
They must be around here somewhere.

847
01:23:08,960 --> 01:23:11,079
But where?

848
01:23:21,560 --> 01:23:29,119
Holofira

849
01:23:44,560 --> 01:23:46,159
Alps!

850
01:23:46,160 --> 01:23:49,519
Kill all of them! Come on

851
01:25:12,480 --> 01:25:16,359
That traitor dog was going to inform them.

852
01:25:16,680 --> 01:25:20,159
It can't be a coincidence that they are here.

853
01:25:20,160 --> 01:25:22,759
Apparently, they are guarding the temple.

854
01:25:22,760 --> 01:25:24,439
Turhan.

855
01:25:24,440 --> 01:25:26,559
Hide the bodies of these dogs.

856
01:25:26,560 --> 01:25:28,879
Yes my Shahzade.
-Oghuz. -My Bey.

857
01:25:29,680 --> 01:25:31,719
Bring the horses.
-Yes my Shahzade.

858
01:25:37,840 --> 01:25:41,679
My Holofira... You are alright, huh?
-I am alright.

859
01:25:46,200 --> 01:25:48,039
Come on Alps! Come on

860
01:26:09,520 --> 01:26:11,799
I have waited a long time for this day.

861
01:26:12,080 --> 01:26:15,719
I will finally see the enemies I
have heard about from my aunt.

862
01:26:15,880 --> 01:26:17,639
I have always imagined it.

863
01:26:17,960 --> 01:26:21,359
If they are bad enough to
kill my mother and father...

864
01:26:21,840 --> 01:26:24,119
...then they are as ugly as that, aren't they?

865
01:26:24,120 --> 01:26:26,559
Or terrifying.

866
01:26:27,840 --> 01:26:31,319
Welcome, Fatma Hatun.
-May it be easy.

867
01:26:31,920 --> 01:26:36,759
Welcome.
-May it be easy.

868
01:26:38,640 --> 01:26:40,439
Thank you.

869
01:26:40,440 --> 01:26:43,919
Osman's daughter, Fatma.

870
01:26:52,080 --> 01:26:54,519
They all look beautiful.

871
01:26:55,440 --> 01:26:59,759
Welcome Bala Hatun. May it be easy. Thank you.

872
01:27:00,200 --> 01:27:04,279
Welcome Bala Hatun...

873
01:27:07,960 --> 01:27:10,199
May Allah bless you. Welcome Bala Hatun.

874
01:27:11,960 --> 01:27:13,879
Don't approach them.

875
01:27:14,360 --> 01:27:16,559
We must be careful.

876
01:27:18,760 --> 01:27:21,519
I will see that horrible woman. -Not now.

877
01:27:24,280 --> 01:27:25,959
Praise be.

878
01:27:29,200 --> 01:27:31,159
Listen to me.

879
01:27:32,440 --> 01:27:34,799
She mustn't see us. Come on.

880
01:27:36,400 --> 01:27:37,639
Not now, Poena

881
01:27:51,040 --> 01:27:53,079
Welcome.

882
01:27:53,920 --> 01:27:57,639
Welcome, Bala Hatun.
-Welcome.

883
01:27:59,280 --> 01:28:03,159
-Thank you.
-Thank you, welcome.

884
01:28:17,160 --> 01:28:18,719
May your work be easy.

885
01:28:19,200 --> 01:28:22,159
-Thank you.
-Thank you, Bala Hatun.

886
01:28:22,320 --> 01:28:24,639
-Daughter.
-Mother.

887
01:28:25,680 --> 01:28:28,639
Thank you. May your work be easy.

888
01:28:37,000 --> 01:28:39,319
She is beautiful.

889
01:28:41,280 --> 01:28:43,479
Come on, come on.

890
01:28:57,000 --> 01:28:59,999
Karesiogullari Beylic

891
01:29:00,400 --> 01:29:03,919
Do I have permission, my Bey? -Come in!

892
01:29:08,800 --> 01:29:10,919
My Bey.
-Yes?

893
01:29:13,000 --> 01:29:15,639
Osman Bey attacked the caravan.

894
01:29:16,720 --> 01:29:20,519
He got all the ores and took the alps captive.

895
01:29:21,320 --> 01:29:25,599
My Bey... Sancar...
-Sancar what?

896
01:29:27,760 --> 01:29:30,159
He killed Sancar too.

897
01:29:31,600 --> 01:29:33,719
Is he dead?

898
01:29:35,720 --> 01:29:37,559
Kanyumaz.

899
01:29:38,640 --> 01:29:40,439
You...

900
01:29:41,360 --> 01:29:45,199
What are you saying, Kanyumaz?
-My Bey...

901
01:29:45,800 --> 01:29:49,719
Osman Bey found out about
your contact with Begum Hatun.

902
01:29:49,920 --> 01:29:52,319
So he imprisoned Begum Hatun.

903
01:29:52,720 --> 01:29:54,639
She will stand trial.

904
01:29:55,000 --> 01:30:01,719
Osman... How did he find out?
-I don't know, my Bey.

905
01:30:04,480 --> 01:30:06,399
Osman.

906
01:30:08,240 --> 01:30:11,599
...will execute Begum Hatun.

907
01:30:11,760 --> 01:30:15,359
Shall I inform our Beys?
Shall we gather the soldiers?

908
01:30:17,240 --> 01:30:21,519
First, we will save Begum Hatun.

909
01:30:21,600 --> 01:30:24,159
I will draw her on my side.

910
01:30:24,800 --> 01:30:26,959
Send a message to Gencer Bey.

911
01:30:27,160 --> 01:30:30,159
Tell him to take Begum Hatun away somehow.

912
01:30:30,320 --> 01:30:32,999
As you order my Bey.

913
01:30:39,560 --> 01:30:43,759
I will drown you in deep waters, Osman.

914
01:30:44,120 --> 01:30:47,359
You will pay a heavy price for this.

915
01:30:47,640 --> 01:30:52,239
You'll pay a heavy price for this.

916
01:31:14,720 --> 01:31:18,319
I am... Are you alright?
I didn't see you were coming.

917
01:31:21,640 --> 01:31:24,679
I'm sorry, Fatma Hatun. My mistake.

918
01:31:24,760 --> 01:31:27,959
But... What will I tell my grandmother now?

919
01:31:28,080 --> 01:31:30,239
I bought this with my last coin.

920
01:31:30,640 --> 01:31:32,439
Don't be upset.

921
01:31:32,960 --> 01:31:34,799
Wait, wait.

922
01:31:35,040 --> 01:31:37,399
-What's your name?
-Meryem.

923
01:31:37,840 --> 01:31:41,799
-Meryem... Did we meet before?
-No, we've moved here recently.

924
01:31:41,920 --> 01:31:45,319
-I'm sorry.
-Wait. Don't be.

925
01:31:45,520 --> 01:31:47,119
It wasn't your mistake.

926
01:31:47,960 --> 01:31:50,399
Let's buy some molasses for you.

927
01:31:50,600 --> 01:31:54,039
No, I can't accept this. It was my mistake.

928
01:31:54,120 --> 01:31:58,119
No way. I accept no objections. Let's go.

929
01:31:59,160 --> 01:32:04,839
-May your work be easy.
-Thank you, Bala Hatun.

930
01:32:05,040 --> 01:32:06,919
There my mother comes.

931
01:32:07,000 --> 01:32:09,599
Even if you object to
me, you can't object to her.

932
01:32:09,680 --> 01:32:14,479
-Another time, Fatma Hatun.
-Stop. Wait.

933
01:32:15,080 --> 01:32:17,479
I owe you one, alright?

934
01:32:20,680 --> 01:32:24,039
My daughter, come here.
-Mother.

935
01:32:38,520 --> 01:32:41,919
Not now. It's too crowded.

936
01:32:42,200 --> 01:32:44,199
Not now. Let's go.

937
01:32:44,480 --> 01:32:46,159
Come on.

938
01:32:52,840 --> 01:32:55,439
This is Sofia's nest, my Shahzade.

939
01:32:55,760 --> 01:32:57,479
It's protected like a castle.

940
01:32:57,680 --> 01:33:00,759
Their den will be their hell, of course.

941
01:33:01,000 --> 01:33:02,599
But first...

942
01:33:03,200 --> 01:33:06,519
...we need to be sure
that this is Sofia's place.

943
01:33:09,080 --> 01:33:11,719
My Shahzade, someone's coming.

944
01:33:18,600 --> 01:33:19,319
Stop!

945
01:33:22,200 --> 01:33:23,799
Search the cart.

946
01:33:38,000 --> 01:33:41,079
Only women can pass. Men have to wait.

947
01:33:45,280 --> 01:33:47,039
Open the gate.

948
01:33:53,920 --> 01:33:55,919
You can go.

949
01:34:05,840 --> 01:34:09,039
I was planning to enter
disguising as priests...

950
01:34:09,080 --> 01:34:11,679
...but they let only women in.

951
01:34:11,840 --> 01:34:13,359
I will go alone.

952
01:34:13,480 --> 01:34:16,639
-They won't notice anything.
-That's not happening.

953
01:34:17,280 --> 01:34:19,879
I can't let you go there alone.

954
01:34:21,200 --> 01:34:24,359
-Orhan.
-It's out of question.

955
01:34:25,200 --> 01:34:27,559
I don't want to hear
any other words.

956
01:34:28,440 --> 01:34:30,399
What will we do, my Shahzade?

957
01:34:30,720 --> 01:34:34,999
If this is Sofia's place,
we shouldn't scare her.

958
01:34:35,480 --> 01:34:39,439
We will prepare well and rush inside.

959
01:34:39,680 --> 01:34:43,319
Now we're going back to the tribe.

960
01:34:43,880 --> 01:34:45,319
Let's go.

961
01:34:58,600 --> 01:35:01,999
We investigated as you ordered
and we found a lead, my Bey.

962
01:35:02,120 --> 01:35:07,759
Some armed people with dark clothes
are entering a monastery near Akhisar.

963
01:35:08,600 --> 01:35:10,839
-They didn't see you, did they?
-No, my Bey.

964
01:35:11,040 --> 01:35:13,159
We observed from a distance.

965
01:35:13,760 --> 01:35:17,639
Byzantine soldiers watch at the gate, my Bey.

966
01:35:17,880 --> 01:35:22,239
Nobody but Christian nuns can go inside.

967
01:35:22,440 --> 01:35:25,239
They let no men in.

968
01:35:25,960 --> 01:35:28,679
If it were for only nuns

969
01:35:29,200 --> 01:35:31,999
..soldiers wouldn't need to watch.

970
01:35:34,120 --> 01:35:39,519
Obviously, they're hiding
someone inside. They are inside.

971
01:35:41,560 --> 01:35:46,239
We can get prepared and attack
the monastery at dawn, but...

972
01:35:46,760 --> 01:35:53,399
...if Sofia's men aren't inside, this
will only bother Orthodox community.

973
01:35:54,800 --> 01:35:57,159
You're right, girl.

974
01:35:57,600 --> 01:36:01,719
That place will be our land soon.

975
01:36:01,880 --> 01:36:05,399
The community of that
monastery will be our people soon.

976
01:36:05,480 --> 01:36:09,999
We shouldn't break their
hearts before we are sure.

977
01:36:11,760 --> 01:36:16,279
Then I will infiltrate into
the monastery first, my Bey.

978
01:36:16,480 --> 01:36:19,574
A few sisters and I will
disguise as Christian nun...

979
01:36:19,586 --> 01:36:22,759
...and enter the monastery
and observe around.

980
01:36:22,760 --> 01:36:23,719
No.

981
01:36:24,520 --> 01:36:26,039
No, Bala.

982
01:36:26,520 --> 01:36:29,359
That demon may show up there.

983
01:36:29,480 --> 01:36:32,239
I can't send you on such a dangerous mission.

984
01:36:32,800 --> 01:36:35,959
Don't you know me, my Bey?

985
01:36:37,760 --> 01:36:41,075
I can enter that monastery,
make them believe I'm...

986
01:36:41,087 --> 01:36:44,279
a Christian nun and
come out of there alive.

987
01:36:49,560 --> 01:36:52,599
Mother, I'm going with you then.

988
01:36:57,520 --> 01:36:59,799
Let me go with you too.

989
01:37:00,200 --> 01:37:04,079
They are my coreligionists. We
will draw less suspicion in this way.

990
01:37:07,160 --> 01:37:08,879
You're right, my dear.

991
01:37:09,160 --> 01:37:12,799
You can speak their language too. Let's go.

992
01:37:13,000 --> 01:37:14,399
Gonca.

993
01:37:15,120 --> 01:37:17,759
You go to Sogut.

994
01:37:18,720 --> 01:37:21,839
The market shouldn't
stay without a head, alright?

995
01:37:44,960 --> 01:37:46,879
Begum Hatun.

996
01:37:47,760 --> 01:37:50,919
Just wait. Wait.

997
01:37:52,080 --> 01:37:54,759
Do I have permission, my Bey?
-Come in!

998
01:37:58,160 --> 01:37:59,719
My Bey.

999
01:38:00,640 --> 01:38:03,439
Stall the sisters carrying the food.

1000
01:38:06,840 --> 01:38:10,479
Change this bread with the other one.

1001
01:38:11,000 --> 01:38:13,879
Don't draw any suspicion.

1002
01:38:13,880 --> 01:38:15,559
My Bey.
-Wait.

1003
01:38:15,760 --> 01:38:18,479
Follow Begum Hatun when she escapes.

1004
01:38:18,520 --> 01:38:22,999
Tell her that Karesi Bey's soldiers
are waiting for him in the north.

1005
01:38:23,160 --> 01:38:26,119
-Alright?
-As you order, my Bey.

1006
01:38:29,000 --> 01:38:31,719
I did my part.

1007
01:38:32,400 --> 01:38:34,239
Begum Hatun.

1008
01:38:35,240 --> 01:38:38,879
The rest is up to your skills.

1009
01:38:42,760 --> 01:38:44,119
Oguz Alp.

1010
01:38:44,440 --> 01:38:47,759
-Let me see my sister.
-No, Yusuf Bey.

1011
01:38:47,920 --> 01:38:49,639
Osman Bey gave strict orders.

1012
01:38:50,000 --> 01:38:53,959
-We can't let anyone in.
Brother, you're making a mistake.

1013
01:38:53,960 --> 01:38:57,319
My sister isn't a traitor. She
didn't betray anyone. Sister!

1014
01:38:57,320 --> 01:39:00,919
Do you hear me, sister?
-Yusuf Bey.

1015
01:39:01,520 --> 01:39:04,679
Raise no difficulties. Go now.

1016
01:39:06,720 --> 01:39:09,199
Okay, brother. Okay.

1017
01:39:09,680 --> 01:39:13,319
I'm here, sister. Don't worry. I will save you!

1018
01:39:13,480 --> 01:39:15,799
Don't worry. I will save you!

1019
01:39:15,800 --> 01:39:17,439
Don't worry

1020
01:39:21,000 --> 01:39:22,679
My brother...

1021
01:39:27,640 --> 01:39:29,839
Here is your food, Begum Hatun.

1022
01:39:31,560 --> 01:39:33,159
Thank you.

1023
01:40:13,160 --> 01:40:16,399
You didn't accept my friendship but...

1024
01:40:16,560 --> 01:40:19,759
...I'm still saving you from the fire.

1025
01:40:20,080 --> 01:40:23,079
You didn't leave me alone, huh, Karesi Bey?

1026
01:40:23,560 --> 01:40:25,959
You sent Kanyumaz for me.

1027
01:40:50,600 --> 01:40:53,479
Sisters! Alps! Come here!

1028
01:41:05,880 --> 01:41:07,839
Begum Hatun.

1029
01:41:08,280 --> 01:41:10,399
You...

1030
01:41:10,840 --> 01:41:13,319
-Gencer Bey's alp. My Bey has sent me.

1031
01:41:13,480 --> 01:41:15,959
Wear those clothes quickly.

1032
01:41:16,080 --> 01:41:18,279
They're waiting for you in the north.

1033
01:41:22,920 --> 01:41:25,039
My pretty-faced wife.

1034
01:41:25,360 --> 01:41:27,479
I believe in you.

1035
01:41:28,080 --> 01:41:29,519
But you need to be careful.

1036
01:41:29,600 --> 01:41:32,279
Of course, Osman. I will be.

1037
01:41:32,840 --> 01:41:36,479
I won't die before seeing Sofia's death.

1038
01:41:37,240 --> 01:41:40,399
About her last words...

1039
01:41:41,880 --> 01:41:46,239
Her last words? You're
thinking about the secret?

1040
01:41:49,160 --> 01:41:51,479
Do I have permission, my Bey?

1041
01:41:52,520 --> 01:41:54,199
Come in!

1042
01:41:59,840 --> 01:42:02,959
Begum Hatun escaped from the cage tent, my Bey.

1043
01:42:10,920 --> 01:42:14,039
Begum Hatun escaped, huh?

1044
01:42:17,640 --> 01:42:20,319
I'm not a traitor!

1045
01:42:22,120 --> 01:42:23,879
I know.

1046
01:42:25,680 --> 01:42:27,999
I know, Begum Hatun.

1047
01:42:31,440 --> 01:42:37,639
When Boran and Cerkutay followed
you, they heard what you told Karesi Bey.

1048
01:42:38,480 --> 01:42:41,479
You said you would never
take Karesi Bey's side.

1049
01:42:42,000 --> 01:42:45,879
-What is this situation then, my Bey?
-That's why you are here.

1050
01:42:47,200 --> 01:42:51,039
To draw no suspicion while
taking Karesi Bey's side.

1051
01:42:51,280 --> 01:42:54,559
He will attempt to save
you and you will go to him.

1052
01:42:55,560 --> 01:42:57,559
And you'll pledge loyalty.

1053
01:42:57,840 --> 01:43:00,279
When he works with the heathens

1054
01:43:01,120 --> 01:43:02,999
...you will inform me.

1055
01:43:03,840 --> 01:43:08,879
When your betrayal is exposed

1056
01:43:10,120 --> 01:43:13,839
...the real traitor will feel easy. So...

1057
01:43:15,920 --> 01:43:18,199
...he will make a mistake.

1058
01:43:19,080 --> 01:43:20,479
And?

1059
01:43:20,720 --> 01:43:25,239
As you ordered, I got all the
beys and their men followed.

1060
01:43:28,280 --> 01:43:31,759
The one who helped Begum Hatun escape...
-Who?

1061
01:43:34,960 --> 01:43:36,919
Gencer, my Bey.

1062
01:43:42,720 --> 01:43:44,599
Gencer, huh?

1063
01:43:50,800 --> 01:43:54,079
Do I have permission, my Bey?
-Come in!

1064
01:43:57,640 --> 01:44:00,359
My Bey, this is Gencer Bey's alp.

1065
01:44:00,480 --> 01:44:03,959
We made him speak. He confessed everything.

1066
01:44:09,720 --> 01:44:12,639
-Take him to the square.
-As you order, my Bey.

1067
01:44:18,960 --> 01:44:21,639
It's you, huh?

1068
01:44:23,920 --> 01:44:25,879
We will see now.

1069
01:44:27,160 --> 01:44:30,199
What are we waiting for? The traitor escaped!

1070
01:44:30,240 --> 01:44:32,239
What will we tell Osman Bey now?

1071
01:44:32,720 --> 01:44:36,119
Let's go after Begum Hatun!
-Bayhan Bey.

1072
01:44:37,640 --> 01:44:41,479
Calm down. Our alps are
following her. Don't worry.

1073
01:44:41,840 --> 01:44:43,359
Besides

1074
01:44:43,680 --> 01:44:49,479
...nobody will step out of the tribe
without Osman Bey's permission.

1075
01:44:49,800 --> 01:44:54,039
My sister isn't a traitor! She
never betrayed Osman Bey!

1076
01:44:55,440 --> 01:44:57,879
But I don't know why she escaped.

1077
01:44:58,640 --> 01:45:01,759
Escaping would mean accepting the disgrace.

1078
01:45:02,440 --> 01:45:05,839
-Why, sister?
-Yusuf.

1079
01:45:06,160 --> 01:45:08,439
You said it yourself.

1080
01:45:08,840 --> 01:45:11,639
Escaping means accepting the guilt.

1081
01:45:11,680 --> 01:45:16,839
Now it's halal for all of
us to kill Begum Hatun!

1082
01:45:19,320 --> 01:45:21,879
Attention! Osman Bey!

1083
01:45:44,080 --> 01:45:46,399
Betrayal...

1084
01:45:47,560 --> 01:45:50,319
...will be punished, of course.

1085
01:45:52,880 --> 01:45:55,239
Although Begum Hatun escaped,

1086
01:45:57,800 --> 01:46:03,319
...the one who helped her
escape is among us now.

1087
01:46:06,680 --> 01:46:11,799
Leave me! Osman Bey! What are you doing?

1088
01:46:12,160 --> 01:46:13,759
Betrayal...

1089
01:46:14,520 --> 01:46:16,639
...is performed secretly.

1090
01:46:17,480 --> 01:46:19,879
But it never stays secret.

1091
01:46:23,080 --> 01:46:25,159
What, Gencer Bey?

1092
01:46:26,080 --> 01:46:29,439
Did you think I wouldn't find
out you were working with Karesi?

1093
01:46:30,120 --> 01:46:32,559
I didn't betray you, Osman Bey.
-Shut up!

1094
01:46:34,040 --> 01:46:35,319
Shut up!

1095
01:46:35,440 --> 01:46:38,679
You keep telling lies by looking into my eyes.

1096
01:46:39,680 --> 01:46:41,959
About the hunt

1097
01:46:43,440 --> 01:46:46,319
...you told Karesi everything I planned.

1098
01:46:47,000 --> 01:46:49,559
You helped Sofia escape from us.

1099
01:46:51,640 --> 01:46:54,879
I started this path taking the risk of death.

1100
01:46:56,200 --> 01:46:58,079
You knew that.

1101
01:46:59,320 --> 01:47:02,159
You knew that but still you betrayed me.

1102
01:47:02,520 --> 01:47:03,879
And also

1103
01:47:04,280 --> 01:47:06,839
...you helped Begum
Hatun escape from the tribe.

1104
01:47:07,240 --> 01:47:08,999
Gencer Bey.

1105
01:47:16,160 --> 01:47:17,679
You disobeyed my orders.

1106
01:47:19,960 --> 01:47:22,079
You violated our laws.

1107
01:47:22,880 --> 01:47:24,399
You betrayed the state.

1108
01:47:27,080 --> 01:47:28,759
My Bey.

1109
01:47:29,400 --> 01:47:31,839
I made a mistake, but forgive me.

1110
01:47:31,840 --> 01:47:34,119
Don't kill me, my Bey. -No.

1111
01:47:36,040 --> 01:47:38,439
Bring him. -My Bey... My Bey...

1112
01:47:45,080 --> 01:47:48,239
You didn't just betray me...

1113
01:47:49,960 --> 01:47:52,399
...you betrayed the state.

1114
01:47:52,960 --> 01:47:55,399
Osman Bey...

1115
01:47:55,400 --> 01:47:57,079
...might forgive.

1116
01:48:00,120 --> 01:48:02,479
But the state...

1117
01:48:04,400 --> 01:48:06,039
...the state never forgives.

1118
01:48:08,160 --> 01:48:09,999
The state..

1119
01:48:10,480 --> 01:48:12,519
...always makes the traitors pay for it.

1120
01:48:14,200 --> 01:48:16,719
Gencer Bey.

1121
01:48:22,680 --> 01:48:24,839
You betrayed your Bey...

1122
01:48:24,840 --> 01:48:26,439
...our laws...

1123
01:48:26,680 --> 01:48:27,839
...and our state.

1124
01:48:34,360 --> 01:48:36,599
Now, the price for this is death.

1125
01:48:55,800 --> 01:49:04,279
I worship except Allah and I bear witness that
Muhammad(PBUH) is His servant and Messenger.

1126
01:49:13,720 --> 01:49:17,319
Divine justice has been served, Osman Bey.

1127
01:49:17,320 --> 01:49:20,599
Thanks to Allah, justice has
been served, Osman Bey.

1128
01:49:21,880 --> 01:49:24,159
This fallen head...

1129
01:49:26,120 --> 01:49:29,279
...is not the first, nor will it
be the last traitor among us.

1130
01:49:31,480 --> 01:49:33,839
Let everyone hear that...

1131
01:49:34,520 --> 01:49:38,519
...anyone who tries to do this again...

1132
01:49:39,280 --> 01:49:42,799
...will face the same fate.

1133
01:50:04,600 --> 01:50:06,679
Poena.

1134
01:50:10,520 --> 01:50:13,959
Did you see your enemies?

1135
01:50:13,960 --> 01:50:16,359
Have you met Bala?

1136
01:50:18,640 --> 01:50:21,079
I feel so bad, aunt.

1137
01:50:22,120 --> 01:50:24,519
I saw them.

1138
01:50:24,520 --> 01:50:27,679
I saw Bala, her daughter.

1139
01:50:29,400 --> 01:50:32,959
What happened? Tell me.

1140
01:50:34,600 --> 01:50:37,919
They stole my family, my life.

1141
01:50:40,040 --> 01:50:42,719
They killed my mother and father.

1142
01:50:43,440 --> 01:50:47,759
But they are still very happy. Is this fair?

1143
01:50:51,240 --> 01:50:52,319
No.

1144
01:50:54,800 --> 01:50:59,919
But you and I will bring
justice, my little bird.

1145
01:50:59,920 --> 01:51:06,479
They will pay for all the pain they caused us.

1146
01:51:06,920 --> 01:51:08,879
You will...

1147
01:51:09,280 --> 01:51:11,199
...take the revenge...

1148
01:51:11,320 --> 01:51:14,879
...of your mother and father.

1149
01:51:18,720 --> 01:51:20,919
Don't cry.

1150
01:51:21,280 --> 01:51:24,079
It's time for revenge.

1151
01:51:26,720 --> 01:51:28,639
Tell me.

1152
01:51:28,640 --> 01:51:32,039
How was your first day on the mission?

1153
01:51:32,040 --> 01:51:35,199
I met Osman's daughter, Fatma.

1154
01:51:36,400 --> 01:51:38,039
I saw Bala.

1155
01:51:39,890 --> 01:51:41,199
How did you...

1156
01:51:42,760 --> 01:51:43,999
..feel when you..

1157
01:51:46,480 --> 01:51:49,319
...first saw her?

1158
01:51:49,620 --> 01:51:51,759
Wrath

1159
01:51:55,040 --> 01:51:56,919
I wanted to kill her...

1160
01:51:57,670 --> 01:51:59,599
...right there.

1161
01:52:04,840 --> 01:52:07,319
Poena.

1162
01:52:11,280 --> 01:52:13,119
Soon...

1163
01:52:15,520 --> 01:52:18,969
...very soon, you will kill her.

1164
01:52:25,120 --> 01:52:28,119
Karacaogullari Beylic

1165
01:52:32,280 --> 01:52:33,879
Can I come in, my Bey?

1166
01:52:34,520 --> 01:52:36,439
Come in.

1167
01:52:46,720 --> 01:52:49,519
We brought Begum Hatun here safely, my Bey.

1168
01:52:52,080 --> 01:52:54,079
Thanks to Allah.

1169
01:52:54,760 --> 01:52:58,119
We saved you from Osman's hands safely.

1170
01:53:02,160 --> 01:53:04,039
As you order, my Bey.

1171
01:53:05,120 --> 01:53:06,519
Thank you Karesi Bey.

1172
01:53:07,000 --> 01:53:10,347
Thanks to you, I can see
what is right and wrong very well.

1173
01:53:10,719 --> 01:53:11,839
I told you.

1174
01:53:12,600 --> 01:53:17,359
Osman is very skilled at executing
people with extreme prejudice.

1175
01:53:17,360 --> 01:53:22,159
He lives far from justice
and is unaware of our laws.

1176
01:53:22,160 --> 01:53:24,039
You are right.

1177
01:53:24,600 --> 01:53:27,519
He didn't even let me speak or defend myself.

1178
01:53:27,740 --> 01:53:29,759
He was going to take me to the gallows.

1179
01:53:30,560 --> 01:53:33,239
They have done you wrong so many times.

1180
01:53:35,560 --> 01:53:39,399
From now on, you are with me.

1181
01:53:40,880 --> 01:53:43,719
Osman can never touch you.

1182
01:53:44,881 --> 01:53:46,320
Never.

1183
01:53:46,520 --> 01:53:50,559
But we must strengthen this with our union.

1184
01:53:53,000 --> 01:53:54,949
What do you mean, Karesi Bey?

1185
01:53:56,720 --> 01:53:59,639
I don't want your
allegiance, Begum Hatun.

1186
01:54:01,550 --> 01:54:02,749
Then..

1187
01:54:03,640 --> 01:54:05,959
...what do you want from me? Why..

1188
01:54:07,080 --> 01:54:09,519
...did you save me, Karesi Bey?

1189
01:54:10,040 --> 01:54:12,159
Begum Hatun...

1190
01:54:14,160 --> 01:54:16,199
I want to marry you.

1191
01:54:21,970 --> 01:54:23,649
Marry me.

1192
01:54:27,850 --> 01:54:29,159
Karesi Bey.

1193
01:54:30,480 --> 01:54:32,599
Be my wife in my house.

1194
01:54:32,600 --> 01:54:35,119
Be my companion on my path...

1195
01:54:35,120 --> 01:54:37,519
...and be the Hatun of my Beylic.

1196
01:54:44,440 --> 01:54:46,359
What do you think?

1197
01:54:49,640 --> 01:54:50,679
Yes...

1198
01:54:51,520 --> 01:54:52,359
...or no?

1199
01:54:56,360 --> 01:54:58,799
I don't know what to say.

1200
01:55:01,960 --> 01:55:04,239
Osman Bey.

1201
01:55:08,880 --> 01:55:12,159
I mean, Osman Bey will pay for it for sure.

1202
01:55:21,440 --> 01:55:24,239
I accept marrying you, Karesi Bey.

1203
01:55:36,530 --> 01:55:38,719
Kanyumaz.

1204
01:55:41,290 --> 01:55:42,759
My Bey.

1205
01:55:43,360 --> 01:55:45,359
Forty rams will be sacrificed.

1206
01:55:45,680 --> 01:55:48,359
Gifts should be given to forty doors.

1207
01:55:49,280 --> 01:55:50,919
Set a full table.

1208
01:55:51,840 --> 01:55:53,479
We will celebrate tomorrow.

1209
01:55:54,320 --> 01:55:55,919
Send news to our Beys.

1210
01:55:57,280 --> 01:55:59,039
Come on! -As you say, my Bey!

1211
01:56:19,720 --> 01:56:21,179
Scholar...

1212
01:56:22,520 --> 01:56:24,559
Be careful.

1213
01:56:25,800 --> 01:56:29,239
Don't upset yourself for
anything Trickster Hatun.

1214
01:56:33,440 --> 01:56:35,399
Attention! Osman Bey!

1215
01:56:41,530 --> 01:56:42,609
My Bala.

1216
01:56:42,960 --> 01:56:46,039
Now I am going to question Karesi Bey for this.

1217
01:56:46,480 --> 01:56:49,719
And you will go and see if
Sofia's men are in the monastery.

1218
01:56:50,320 --> 01:56:52,519
But don't make a move before I come.

1219
01:56:53,120 --> 01:56:54,239
Don't worry my Bey.

1220
01:56:55,120 --> 01:56:57,919
Come on, children! We will leave first!

1221
01:57:01,120 --> 01:57:04,239
-Is our gift ready?
-Yes my Bey.

1222
01:57:05,120 --> 01:57:08,479
It was prepared with care
for Karesi Bey, my Bey.

1223
01:57:09,700 --> 01:57:15,679
We won't go empty-handed even to Karesi Bey,
who shows a friendly face and bears hostility.

1224
01:57:15,680 --> 01:57:17,319
It is our tradition.

1225
01:57:17,320 --> 01:57:19,479
Of course, we'll go there with our gift.

1226
01:57:19,840 --> 01:57:23,239
Kayi is both the hammer and the anvil.

1227
01:57:27,440 --> 01:57:29,319
We will show Karesi Bey that.

1228
01:57:30,280 --> 01:57:31,919
To horses!

1229
01:58:01,960 --> 01:58:07,439
Do you really have to see Lukas and
Sofia and trade with them Karesi Bey?

1230
01:58:08,840 --> 01:58:11,079
They tried to kill my brother.

1231
01:58:11,880 --> 01:58:14,359
I know.

1232
01:58:15,440 --> 01:58:18,919
They will apologize to you for this.

1233
01:58:20,920 --> 01:58:23,199
And they will do it today.

1234
01:58:25,650 --> 01:58:27,799
I invited them for dinner.

1235
01:58:31,510 --> 01:58:33,309
Don't be upset...

1236
01:58:34,160 --> 01:58:37,959
In the end, you are the Hatun of Karesi Beylic.

1237
01:58:37,960 --> 01:58:40,439
Who can stand against you?

1238
01:58:40,840 --> 01:58:41,639
Besides...

1239
01:58:41,880 --> 01:58:46,439
...we will be stronger thanks to
our alliance with Lukas and Sofia.

1240
01:58:46,880 --> 01:58:50,839
Osman will eventually kneel before us.

1241
01:58:53,040 --> 01:58:56,399
I guess this will not be an eternal alliance.

1242
01:58:57,120 --> 01:59:01,359
I always consider my own
interests, Begum Hatun.

1243
01:59:02,280 --> 01:59:04,839
I will use Lukas and Sofia...

1244
01:59:06,520 --> 01:59:10,599
...and soon, I will throw them away.

1245
01:59:12,680 --> 01:59:14,719
Come here.

1246
01:59:22,160 --> 01:59:27,679
From now on, half of my
ships will be under your control.

1247
01:59:28,200 --> 01:59:29,439
Also...

1248
01:59:32,160 --> 01:59:34,519
...as a wedding gift...

1249
01:59:37,080 --> 01:59:41,439
...the most glorious one
of my castles will be yours.

1250
01:59:42,360 --> 01:59:43,959
Thank you Karesi Bey.

1251
01:59:44,440 --> 01:59:45,359
Live long.

1252
01:59:46,640 --> 01:59:49,959
I haven't forgotten your brother Yusuf either.

1253
01:59:50,240 --> 01:59:53,719
I will let him be the Commander of my armies.

1254
01:59:54,240 --> 01:59:56,799
He must be mad at me right now.

1255
01:59:57,680 --> 02:00:00,639
But he will understand me for sure.

1256
02:00:01,680 --> 02:00:05,239
He will learn what his sister has sacrificed.

1257
02:00:20,240 --> 02:00:22,879
Karesi Bey is marrying Begum Hatun.

1258
02:00:23,440 --> 02:00:24,879
Begum Hatun?

1259
02:00:28,520 --> 02:00:31,039
She was very loyal to Osman.

1260
02:00:31,840 --> 02:00:33,919
It seems she loves Karesi more.

1261
02:00:37,560 --> 02:00:40,039
He invites us to the celebration meal.

1262
02:00:42,280 --> 02:00:44,639
We will go to that meal, Lukas.

1263
02:00:45,320 --> 02:00:49,239
To strengthen our alliance with Karesi Bey.

1264
02:00:51,720 --> 02:00:53,879
We will go there.

1265
02:01:51,280 --> 02:01:53,639
Wait, you can't come in.

1266
02:02:09,800 --> 02:02:13,119
Open the door.

1267
02:02:19,120 --> 02:02:21,159
Come in.

1268
02:03:36,650 --> 02:03:37,879
Mother...

1269
02:03:37,880 --> 02:03:39,519
Mother what happened?

1270
02:03:39,520 --> 02:03:41,039
Mother?

1271
02:03:41,040 --> 02:03:42,799
What happened? Are you alright?

1272
02:03:42,800 --> 02:03:44,879
Mother...

1273
02:03:44,880 --> 02:03:47,119
Are you alright?

1274
02:03:51,260 --> 02:03:52,679
I am alright.

1275
02:03:52,680 --> 02:03:54,519
I am alright, my daughter.

1276
02:03:55,160 --> 02:03:56,999
Let's take a look around.

1277
02:03:57,000 --> 02:03:59,639
It will be necessary for our move.

1278
02:04:25,480 --> 02:04:27,399
As we thought, my daughter...

1279
02:04:27,400 --> 02:04:28,639
This is Sofia's nest.

1280
02:04:29,360 --> 02:04:31,639
Her soldiers are here.

1281
02:04:32,170 --> 02:04:33,999
This place is well hidden.

1282
02:04:34,560 --> 02:04:37,799
But we solved their secret, thank Allah.

1283
02:04:37,880 --> 02:04:39,879
Come on.

1284
02:04:44,520 --> 02:04:46,319
My Beys.

1285
02:04:47,520 --> 02:04:49,359
Hatuns.

1286
02:04:49,360 --> 02:04:53,359
On this happy day of mine, you
accepted our invitation and came.

1287
02:04:53,960 --> 02:04:55,559
You have shared our meal.

1288
02:04:56,240 --> 02:04:58,239
-Live long.
-Thank you.

1289
02:04:59,430 --> 02:05:01,279
This feast..

1290
02:05:02,400 --> 02:05:09,079
...is in honor of my future wife, Begum
Hatun, who has expanded my home and palace...

1291
02:05:09,520 --> 02:05:11,519
...by joining our side.

1292
02:05:13,120 --> 02:05:14,639
Her presence will...

1293
02:05:15,200 --> 02:05:18,919
...give strength to both me
and our state, God willing.

1294
02:05:19,429 --> 02:05:22,129
God willing, my Bey.

1295
02:05:23,760 --> 02:05:25,719
Thank you, Karesi Bey.

1296
02:05:26,680 --> 02:05:33,559
It is an honor for me to be under the same
roof and in the same gathering with you.

1297
02:05:34,440 --> 02:05:36,359
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

1298
02:05:37,520 --> 02:05:40,959
Then, enjoy your meal.

1299
02:05:44,880 --> 02:05:46,839
My Bey, Osman Bey came.

1300
02:05:48,400 --> 02:05:51,439
Alps, let him in.

1301
02:05:53,280 --> 02:05:56,119
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

1302
02:05:57,720 --> 02:05:59,999
Come, Osman, come.

1303
02:06:00,680 --> 02:06:04,399
You've heard that
I am marrying Begum Hatun...

1304
02:06:04,400 --> 02:06:07,039
...and even brought a gift.

1305
02:06:07,400 --> 02:06:09,479
Right.

1306
02:06:10,560 --> 02:06:12,639
Have you married Begum Hatun?

1307
02:06:18,760 --> 02:06:24,679
Someone like you, who betrays
her state would only deserve this man.

1308
02:06:25,520 --> 02:06:29,359
Osman, you came to my castle and now...

1309
02:06:29,400 --> 02:06:34,039
...are insulting me and my future
wife in the presence of my Beys!

1310
02:06:34,280 --> 02:06:35,319
I am!

1311
02:06:41,200 --> 02:06:46,119
I call a traitor a traitor
and a treacher a treacher.

1312
02:06:50,640 --> 02:06:52,399
Karesi Bey.

1313
02:06:52,840 --> 02:06:54,759
So that the Beys are here...

1314
02:06:56,230 --> 02:06:57,999
...they should all hear it.

1315
02:06:58,680 --> 02:07:02,079
Let them all hear the
treachery you have committed.

1316
02:07:03,810 --> 02:07:05,159
Beys.

1317
02:07:05,630 --> 02:07:07,749
Tell me.

1318
02:07:09,000 --> 02:07:11,439
This careless man...

1319
02:07:11,440 --> 02:07:15,519
...whom you call a ruler and stand behind...

1320
02:07:16,440 --> 02:07:20,359
...sold the steel of the swords
that would kill our Alps...

1321
02:07:20,720 --> 02:07:23,439
...to infidels!

1322
02:07:26,600 --> 02:07:29,399
-Karesi Bey would never do that.
-He did it.

1323
02:07:30,080 --> 02:07:32,119
He did it.

1324
02:07:33,000 --> 02:07:36,239
This careless man you stand behind...

1325
02:07:36,440 --> 02:07:38,079
Shame on you

1326
02:07:40,040 --> 02:07:43,159
Osman... Enough! -No!

1327
02:07:44,160 --> 02:07:46,519
No, Karesi Bey!

1328
02:07:47,800 --> 02:07:48,959
Wait...

1329
02:07:49,930 --> 02:07:51,649
Boran. -My Bey.

1330
02:07:52,160 --> 02:07:54,079
Take this to Karesi Bey.

1331
02:07:58,200 --> 02:07:59,079
No.

1332
02:08:00,600 --> 02:08:03,119
Put it next to him, right next to him.

1333
02:08:13,440 --> 02:08:14,999
Open it, Karesi Bey.

1334
02:08:16,120 --> 02:08:17,239
Open it.

1335
02:08:19,470 --> 02:08:21,139
Open it!

1336
02:08:26,720 --> 02:08:29,599
-How could you do this, Osman!
-This!

1337
02:08:31,080 --> 02:08:32,999
An eye for an eye..

1338
02:08:33,000 --> 02:08:36,039
...a tooth for a tooth!

1339
02:08:41,320 --> 02:08:42,279
So...

1340
02:08:43,730 --> 02:08:47,599
...you sent this traitor to our side, huh?

1341
02:08:48,020 --> 02:08:49,879
Here is his head.

1342
02:08:52,200 --> 02:08:55,359
Now, I have the decree! You...

1343
02:08:55,880 --> 02:08:58,839
...that traitor, and everyone behind you...

1344
02:08:59,440 --> 02:09:00,279
Now...

1345
02:09:01,760 --> 02:09:03,679
Now we are all in war with you.

1346
02:09:08,360 --> 02:09:12,479
Did you think you could come
here and leave this place alive?

1347
02:09:12,720 --> 02:09:14,759
Osman

1348
02:09:17,480 --> 02:09:19,559
My Bey!

1349
02:09:20,690 --> 02:09:22,199
Alps!

1350
02:09:22,800 --> 02:09:26,559
Kill all of them

1351
02:09:31,640 --> 02:09:34,559
You draw a sword against me? Come to me.

1352
02:09:34,760 --> 02:09:36,839
What you have done is enough!

1353
02:09:39,960 --> 02:09:44,959
Alps, stop! Stop, stop.

1354
02:09:47,240 --> 02:09:51,919
We will get out just like
how we got inside.

1355
02:09:52,720 --> 02:09:54,119
Alps!

1356
02:09:55,120 --> 02:09:56,959
Kanyumaz.

1357
02:09:57,440 --> 02:09:59,799
Catch him.

1358
02:10:01,800 --> 02:10:03,759
Move.

1359
02:10:23,320 --> 02:10:26,839
-Tell them to clear the way.
-Move aside. Come on!

1360
02:10:29,080 --> 02:10:30,919
Move.

1361
02:10:31,040 --> 02:10:33,559
Move aside!

1362
02:10:37,600 --> 02:10:39,679
Run with my call.

1363
02:10:39,680 --> 02:10:42,519
This will reinforce your
credibility for Karesi.

1364
02:10:45,160 --> 02:10:47,639
Alps, stop!

1365
02:10:48,280 --> 02:10:50,599
Lower the spears!

1366
02:10:53,400 --> 02:10:55,119
Now.

1367
02:10:58,600 --> 02:11:01,399
You will pay for what you did, Osman Bey!

1368
02:11:02,600 --> 02:11:06,359
But not now. Karesi Bey is
wounded. Let's go, Kanyumaz.

1369
02:11:37,840 --> 02:11:39,879
-Orhan.
-Mother.

1370
02:11:40,280 --> 02:11:43,959
We've found Sofia's nest. Soldiers are inside.

1371
02:11:44,320 --> 02:11:48,279
-Thanks to Allah.
-They are too many.

1372
02:11:49,720 --> 02:11:52,039
When my Bey arrives,

1373
02:11:52,880 --> 02:11:55,959
...we will destroy them all, God willing.

1374
02:11:56,160 --> 02:11:57,399
God willing.

1375
02:11:57,400 --> 02:12:00,119
We should wait now. They shouldn't see us.

1376
02:12:19,840 --> 02:12:24,479
My lady, some Turks have
been detected around the temple.

1377
02:12:26,840 --> 02:12:32,719
-Poena...
They may be making a game.

1378
02:12:33,800 --> 02:12:37,919
Soldiers, we're going to
the temple now! Come on!

1379
02:13:20,880 --> 02:13:22,959
This is enough. Stop.

1380
02:13:25,760 --> 02:13:27,479
Very soon

1381
02:13:27,920 --> 02:13:33,039
...I will bring the death to those
barbarians who slaughtered my family.

1382
02:13:43,960 --> 02:13:46,479
Bala, what is the situation?

1383
02:13:46,640 --> 02:13:52,279
My Bey, this is Sofia's place. We're sure now.

1384
02:13:57,400 --> 02:13:59,319
All her men are inside, my Bey.

1385
02:13:59,480 --> 02:14:03,599
But there are priestesses
and women inside, my Bey.

1386
02:14:03,600 --> 02:14:07,799
Dastards are hiding behind them.

1387
02:14:11,160 --> 02:14:17,119
When we enter the temple,
we'll kill all Sofia's men.

1388
02:14:18,000 --> 02:14:23,199
But, my girl, you will take priestesses
and women somewhere safe.

1389
02:14:23,240 --> 02:14:24,919
As you order, my Bey.

1390
02:14:25,960 --> 02:14:30,159
Boran and Cerkutay are lying
in ambush around the temple.

1391
02:14:30,680 --> 02:14:34,639
When we attack, Sofia
won't get any news about it.

1392
02:14:35,160 --> 02:14:40,999
We'll attack the temple and Sofia will
come to us without knowing anything.

1393
02:14:41,920 --> 02:14:44,399
We'll just wait for our prey, huh, my Bey?

1394
02:14:44,520 --> 02:14:46,039
Absolutely.

1395
02:14:46,240 --> 02:14:48,719
We'll hunt her in her own place.

1396
02:14:51,160 --> 02:14:55,759
Bala, my daughter. You go to
the gate and provide security there.

1397
02:14:57,560 --> 02:15:00,639
May Allah bless our fight!
-Aameen.

1398
02:15:03,640 --> 02:15:05,119
Let's go, girl.

1399
02:15:43,920 --> 02:15:46,559
Open this! Hurry up!

1400
02:15:47,440 --> 02:15:49,199
Open this!

1401
02:15:49,640 --> 02:15:52,839
I should take Poena out
before they know everything

1402
02:15:53,160 --> 02:15:55,839
Open! Open

1403
02:15:56,120 --> 02:15:58,039
We'll arrive in time, Sofia.

1404
02:16:02,640 --> 02:16:04,559
Before they know everything,

1405
02:16:04,840 --> 02:16:06,479
...I should take Poena out.

1406
02:16:07,120 --> 02:16:08,759
Come on.

1407
02:16:29,880 --> 02:16:32,239
Come on!

1408
02:16:34,280 --> 02:16:35,919
Come on

1409
02:16:38,400 --> 02:16:41,079
I made a monster out of Poena.

1410
02:16:41,240 --> 02:16:43,359
If Osman gets her,

1411
02:16:43,638 --> 02:16:45,477
...everything will be ruined.

1412
02:16:45,718 --> 02:16:47,239
He won't, Sofia.

1413
02:16:47,520 --> 02:16:50,638
That monster will be their death.

1414
02:17:02,000 --> 02:17:04,919
Come this way.
Nobody will hurt you.

1415
02:17:05,440 --> 02:17:07,558
This way, come on.

1416
02:17:12,558 --> 02:17:14,679
-Behind you.
-You got this.

1417
02:17:20,799 --> 02:17:21,959
Osman.

1418
02:17:22,080 --> 02:17:24,839
-Osman!
-You got this.

1419
02:17:29,320 --> 02:17:30,839
Bala.

1420
02:17:31,200 --> 02:17:33,119
Bala!

1421
02:17:41,000 --> 02:17:42,919
Let's go.

1422
02:17:43,080 --> 02:17:45,919
-Brother!
-Alaaddin!

1423
02:17:48,638 --> 02:17:50,759
Orhan and Alaaddin.

1424
02:17:56,240 --> 02:17:58,159
Their children.

1425
02:18:01,080 --> 02:18:03,159
Come on, brother!

1426
02:18:04,360 --> 02:18:06,759
Today is the day of vengeance.

1427
02:18:06,959 --> 02:18:10,119
You will pay for what I suffered!

1428
02:18:35,879 --> 02:18:37,759
Die!

1429
02:18:51,160 --> 02:18:54,439
Swing your swords and break the demon's army!

1430
02:19:08,160 --> 02:19:11,397
You will die for your family, Osman.

1431
02:19:11,680 --> 02:19:13,879
Osman

1432
02:19:14,959 --> 02:19:16,959
Aunt.

1433
02:19:17,638 --> 02:19:20,879
-I'm here!
Take Poena out of here!

1434
02:19:24,558 --> 02:19:29,599
This temple you stained with your steps
will be cleaned with your blood, Osman.

1435
02:19:29,600 --> 02:19:33,959
You demon's dog. Your dirt
can be cleaned only in hell.

1436
02:19:39,840 --> 02:19:41,359
Sofia.

1437
02:19:42,080 --> 02:19:44,558
Let's unseal your tongue.

1438
02:19:44,959 --> 02:19:47,759
You remember, huh?

1439
02:19:47,920 --> 02:19:51,079
I will kill you not once but a thousand times.

1440
02:19:51,280 --> 02:19:54,799
Then tell me now. Or you will just pass away.

1441
02:19:59,000 --> 02:20:01,039
Aunt.

1442
02:20:10,800 --> 02:20:12,359
You're dead

1443
02:20:12,640 --> 02:20:15,199
You're a dead man, Osman.

1444
02:20:15,400 --> 02:20:17,679
You can't run away this time.

1445
02:20:36,240 --> 02:20:38,159
Come.

1446
02:20:45,080 --> 02:20:46,959
Osman

1447
02:20:55,760 --> 02:20:57,839
Father!

1448
02:21:03,720 --> 02:21:04,919
My Bey!

1449
02:21:05,400 --> 02:21:06,439
My Bey!

1450
02:21:11,369 --> 02:21:12,659
Die.